          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-fundamental-group-of-the-circle",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "$\\operatorname{Deg}:\\pi_1(\\mathbb R/\\mathbb Z,[0])\\to(\\mathbb Z,+)$ is an isomorphism. Its inverse is\n\n$$n\\longmapsto[\\omega_n].$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-fundamental-group-of-a-product",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For pointed topological spaces $(X,x_0)$ and $(Y,y_0)$, the coordinate projections induce a natural group isomorphism\n\n$$\\Theta:\\pi_1(X\\times Y,(x_0,y_0))\\longrightarrow\\pi_1(X,x_0)\\times\\pi_1(Y,y_0),\\qquad [\\gamma]\\longmapsto([\\pi_X\\gamma],[\\pi_Y\\gamma]).$$\n\nIts inverse sends $([\\alpha],[\\beta])$ to the class of the paired loop $s\\mapsto(\\alpha(s),\\beta(s))$.",
          "uses": [
