          "quote": "Let $P$ be a compact smooth manifold with boundary, let $N$ be a boundaryless Hausdorff smooth manifold, and let $i:P\\to N$ be a smooth embedding. Let $Z\\subset N$ be a closed embedded smooth submanifold without boundary. If $i$ is transverse to $Z$ along $\\partial P$, then an arbitrarily small jointly smooth ambient isotopy, supported in any prescribed neighborhood of $i(P)$ and fixed on a neighborhood of $i(\\partial P)$, makes $i(P)$ transverse to $Z$. The isotopy may be stationary near its time endpoints. No choice axiom is assumed. The same assertion holds for any finite family of such $Z$, provided the initial boundary restriction is transverse to every member. Empty source and empty intersection are allowed.",
