          "quote": "Two smooth circle-bundle fibrations of the same torus with equal unoriented primitive fiber class are carried to one another by a jointly smooth isotopy of the torus starting at the identity and stationary near its time endpoints.\n\nConsequently, suppose two boundary tori of compact smooth Seifert pieces are glued by a specified smooth diffeomorphism and their regular-fiber slopes agree under that identification. The fibrations may be modified by smooth ambient isotopies in arbitrarily small boundary collars so that they agree fiber by fiber on the identified torus and have matching product collar charts there. Their union is then a smooth Seifert fibration of the glued manifold. The two boundary tori may belong to the same piece. For finitely many disjoint matched boundary pairs, the modifications may be performed simultaneously in disjoint collars.",
