        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Remove a small neighborhood of the exceptional point from the annulus base. The remaining pair of pants has fundamental group freely generated by a loop $a$ around the outer boundary and a loop $c$ around the removed cone point; its third boundary loop is $(ac)^{-1}$. The circle bundle over this pair of pants has a section: it retracts to a graph, and a section over that graph is obtained by choosing one point in the fiber at the vertex and extending over each edge. Thus its group has generators $a,c,h$, with $h$ the fiber and $[a,h]=[c,h]=1$. The order-two local model $(z,w)\\mapsto(-z,-w)$ around the exceptional core identifies the filled meridian with $c^2h$ after replacing $c$ by $ch^k$ if necessary: one circuit of the cone-point boundary lifts from $(z,w)$ to $(-z,-w)$, so two circuits equal one inverse fiber turn, and the twisting coefficient is odd. Filling that neighborhood kills this meridian. By [F3],\n$$\n\\pi_1(X_{P_{2,1}})=\\langle a,c,h\\mid [a,h]=[c,h]=1,\\ c^2h=1\\rangle.\n$$\nIts quotient by $\\langle h\\rangle$ is $\\mathbb Z*C_2$, which is nonabelian by reduced normal forms [F4]; hence $X_{P_{2,1}}$ is not $T^2\\times I$. Its outer boundary subgroup is generated by $a,h$. The abelianization is free on $[a],[c]$ with $[h]=-2[c]$, so $a^m h^n=1$ implies $m=0$ and $n=0$. Thus the outer torus group injects into $\\pi_1(X_{P_{2,1}})$ and has no compressing disk.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F3",
            "F4",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra",
            "construct"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-3",
          "claim": "For the trefoil, [F2] gives $\\pi_1(E_K)=\\langle x,y\\mid x^2=y^3\\rangle$ and regular fiber $h_K=x^2=y^3$. Its quotient by $\\langle h_K\\rangle$ is $C_2*C_3$, nonabelian by [F4], and $h_K$ is infinite because its abelianization is $6$ times the generator of $H_1(E_K)\\cong\\mathbb Z$. The group maps onto $S_3$ by $x\\mapsto(12)$ and $y\\mapsto(123)$, so it is nonabelian and $K$ is not the unknot, whose exterior group is $\\mathbb Z$.",
          "step": "1.3",
          "inputs": [
