          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The peripheral formula in [F2] gives $h_K=\\lambda_K+6\\mu_K$. The companion embedding identifies $(\\mu_V,\\lambda_V)$ with $(\\mu_K,\\lambda_K)$. Therefore the two Seifert fibrations on the cut sides induce slopes $2\\lambda+\\mu$ and $\\lambda+6\\mu$ on the companion torus. Their determinant in the ordered basis $(\\mu,\\lambda)$ is $\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&6\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=-11$, so the slopes are not parallel.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
