          "quote": "Let $n\\ge1$.\n\n1. Let $A\\in M_n(\\mathbb Z)$ and let $L=A\\mathbb Z^n\\subseteq\\mathbb Z^n$ be the subgroup generated by the columns of $A$. If $\\det A\\ne0$, then the quotient group $\\mathbb Z^n/L$ is finite of order $\\lvert\\det A\\rvert$; if $\\det A=0$, then $\\mathbb Z^n/L$ is infinite.\n2. Every subgroup $L\\subseteq\\mathbb Z^n$ is $A\\mathbb Z^n$ for some $A\\in M_n(\\mathbb Z)$.\n\nSo a subgroup of $\\mathbb Z^n$ has finite index exactly when it is generated by the columns of a square integer matrix of nonzero determinant, and its index is then the absolute determinant of every such matrix.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
