        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "The pairing map over $\\mathbb Q$ is the composite $H_2(W;\\mathbb Q)\\to H_2(W,M;\\mathbb Q)\\xrightarrow{\\operatorname{PD}^{-1}}H^2(W;\\mathbb Q)\\to\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb Q}(H_2(W;\\mathbb Q),\\mathbb Q)$. Every map in this composite is an isomorphism by step 1.1, [F2], and [F3], so the form is rationally nondegenerate.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
