        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "By [F4] and [A1], $H_2(W;\\mathbb Z)$ is finitely generated, so its torsion-free quotient is a finite-rank free abelian group. If $x$ has finite order $m$, bilinearity gives $mQ_W(x,y)=Q_W(mx,y)=0$ in $\\mathbb Z$, hence $Q_W(x,y)=0$; the same argument applies in the other variable. Thus the form descends to the torsion-free quotient. The four-dimensional cup-product sign is $(-1)^{2\\cdot2}=+1$, so the form is symmetric.",
