          "claim": "**The actual BPST bundle and almost solution.** Fix $p\\in X$ and oriented normal coordinates, with $g_{ij}=\\delta_{ij}+O(r^2)$. In quaternionic coordinates the regular BPST potential is $I_\\lambda=\\operatorname{Im}(q\\,d\\bar q)/(\\lambda^2+|q|^2)$. Write $q=rv$, $|v|=1$, and $\\theta=v\\,d\\bar v$, so $d\\theta=-\\theta\\wedge\\theta$. Differentiation gives $F_{I_\\lambda}=\\lambda^2(\\lambda^2+r^2)^{-2}\\operatorname{Im}(dq\\wedge d\\bar q)$, which is self-dual in the oriented Euclidean metric. Its Euclidean norm square is $48\\lambda^4/(\\lambda^2+r^2)^4$, with integral $8\\pi^2$, and its three curvature components at zero span $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$. Gauge transformation by $v$ gives the singular potential $\\lambda^2(\\lambda^2+r^2)^{-1}\\bar v\\,dv$, bounded by $C\\lambda^2/r^3$ when $r\\ge\\lambda$. Fix a small coordinate radius $\\rho$, independent of $\\lambda$, cut off this singular potential on $\\rho<r<2\\rho$ to zero, and use the regular frame inside. The fixed transition $v$ on their overlap constructs one smooth bundle $P'$ independent of $\\lambda$ and smooth connections $A_\\lambda$ which equal the product connection outside the chart. It is this singular potential that is cut off; a cutoff of a regular potential is not assumed to commute with a gauge transformation.",
