          "source": "def-asd-moduli-fredholm-index-and-lattice-setup",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $X$ be a closed oriented Riemannian four-manifold and let $P\\to X$ be a smooth principal $SU(2)$-bundle with $c_2(P)[X]=-1$. The Hodge star on two-forms is $*$, and $F_A^-=(F_A-*F_A)/2$ denotes the anti-self-dual projection of the curvature of a connection $A$. The equation used in this item is $F_A^-=0$, so the curvature is self-dual; this convention and the negative second Chern number are fixed together for the positive-definite orientation. The self-dual moduli set is the set of smooth connections satisfying $F_A^-=0$, modulo the action of smooth gauge transformations of $P$. At a solution, the deformation complex is $0\\to\\Omega^0(X;\\operatorname{ad}P)\\xrightarrow{d_A}\\Omega^1(X;\\operatorname{ad}P)\\xrightarrow{d_A^-}\\Omega^-(X;\\operatorname{ad}P)\\to0$, and its gauge-fixed operator is $D_A=d_A^*\\oplus d_A^-$. For index calculations, $D_A$ is completed from the first Sobolev space of one-forms to the direct sum of the zeroth Sobolev spaces of zero-forms and anti-self-dual two-forms.",
          "uses": [
