          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-integral-intersection-lattice-of-a-simply-connected-four-manifold",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $X$ be a closed connected oriented smooth four-manifold. Its integral intersection lattice is the abelian group $L_X=H_2(X;\\mathbb Z)/\\operatorname{Tor}H_2(X;\\mathbb Z)$ with the integer-valued symmetric bilinear pairing $Q_X(\\bar x,\\bar y)=\\langle \\operatorname{PD}^{-1}(x)\\smile\\operatorname{PD}^{-1}(y),[X]\\rangle$. Here $\\operatorname{Tor}$ is the subgroup of elements of finite order, $[X]\\in H_4(X;\\mathbb Z)$ is the orientation class, and $\\operatorname{PD}:H^2(X;\\mathbb Z)\\to H_2(X;\\mathbb Z)$ is the Poincaré duality isomorphism. The rank is $b_2(X)=\\dim_{\\mathbb Q}H_2(X;\\mathbb Q)$. The lattice is positive definite when $Q_X(x,x)>0$ for every nonzero $x\\in L_X$; it is unimodular when a Gram matrix in an integral basis has determinant $1$ or $-1$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
