          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "By [F3], $D$ is a smooth proper slice disk; [F1] and [F2] then give a compact rational homology four-ball $B_D$ with boundary $M=\\Sigma_2(K)$. The boundary identification in the statement permits the smooth oriented gluing $X=W\\cup_M(-B_D)$; collars [F7] give a smooth closed oriented four-manifold.",
