          "source": "lem-signed-relative-surface-cut-and-horizontal-decomposition",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "An actual good decomposing surface admits an adapted admissible nice diagram. For a specified coherent orientation class on the exterior complex, the outer summand of that diagram is integrally chain isomorphic to the cut diagram with the induced orientation class; nonzero periodic domains are retained by pullback of characters. When the surface separates into two balanced pieces, every generator is outer and the full complex is identified with the graded tensor product of the two component complexes. In particular the usual two-piece horizontal decomposition has this chain formula. It gives the homology tensor formula over every field; over the integers it gives the graded Künneth exact sequence including Tor.",
