          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $E$ be the compact exterior and $(M,\\gamma)$ its cut along $F$. Its two faces are copies of $F$, and its vertical boundary is the annulus $\\partial F\\times I$. It is balanced: both faces have Euler characteristic $1-2g$, no component is closed, and every boundary component meets the vertical annulus. A meridian intersects $F$ algebraically once, so $F$ is nonseparating and the cut is connected.",
