          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let a compact smooth pair $(M,S)$ without boundary of dimension three or four have $S$ of codimension two, and supply finite branched charts $(y,w)\\mapsto(y,w^2)$ with group $\\mathbb Z/2$ acting by $w\\mapsto-w$, together with their compatible coordinate lifts. Supply a smooth orbifold metric and an $SO(3)$ bundle in these charts with nontrivial isotropy a rotation by $\\pi$ about a line. Use its determinant-one gauge transformations: in each local quaternionic lift they obey $u(y,-w)=\\rho u(y,w)\\rho^{-1}$, where $\\rho=\\operatorname{diag}(i,-i)$ and $\\rho^2=-1$. These conjugation conditions are independent of the sign of the lift.\n\nFinite-chart invariant Sobolev spaces $H^k$ are Hilbert spaces with smooth invariant density, compact $H^{k+1}\\hookrightarrow H^k$ inclusion, and the usual dimension-three or dimension-four Sobolev product and embedding estimates. For $k\\ge3$, the $H^{k+1}$ determinant-one gauge group is a Banach Lie group acting smoothly on the affine $H^k$ connection space. At an irreducible connection, Coulomb slices give a smooth unbased quotient and equation bundle; arbitrary connecting gauges between converging slice representatives have converging $H^{k+1}$ subsequences, up to their central ambiguity.\n\nEvery smooth first-order operator with scalar Clifford square, acting on these bundles and respecting the invariant local conditions, is Fredholm $H^k\\to H^{k-1}$ on compact $M$. Its kernel and cokernel are smooth. A formally selfadjoint such operator $H$ has domain $H^1$ in $L^2$, compact resolvent and a complete real discrete spectrum of finite multiplicity. In particular this applies to the extended three-dimensional Hessian $H_B(\\phi,b)=(d_B^*b,d_B\\phi+*d_Bb)$, and in dimension four to $d_A^*\\oplus\\sqrt2d_A^+$.\n\nOn an infinite cylinder over the compact three-dimensional pair, suppose $H(t)$ has one fixed first-order principal part, shared by $H_\\pm$, throughout the cylinder and differs from