          "quote": "For a smooth real function $f$, its **Riemannian gradient** is $\\operatorname{grad}_g f=(df)^\\sharp$.\n\n[[prop-exterior-derivative-of-a-function-is-its-differential]] identifies $df(X)=Xf$. The smooth bundle isomorphism in [[thm-the-musical-maps-are-smooth-inverse-bundle-isomorphisms]] therefore makes the gradient a smooth vector field. In coordinates $(\\operatorname{grad}_g f)^i=\\sum_jg^{ij}\\partial_jf$. Constants, and all functions in dimension zero, have zero gradient.",
