          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "There is a constant $C_P$ such that $\\|w\\|_{L^2(M)}\\leq C_P\\|\\nabla w\\|_{L^2(M)}$ for $w\\in H_0^1(M)$. Otherwise choose $w_j\\in H_0^1(M)$ with $\\|w_j\\|_{L^2}=1$ and $\\|\\nabla w_j\\|_{L^2}\\to0$. The sequence is bounded in $H^1$. A finite chart partition and [F2] give an $L^2$-convergent subsequence; a further subsequence converges weakly in the Hilbert space $H^1$, so its limit $w$ belongs to the weakly closed subspace $H_0^1(M)$, has weak gradient zero, and has $L^2$ norm one. In each connected coordinate ball, convolution of a function with zero weak gradient is constant on smaller balls; overlapping balls force the constants to agree, so connectedness makes $w$ constant on $M^\\circ$. Its trace is zero by [F4], whereas the trace of a nonzero constant is that same nonzero constant on the nonempty boundary. This contradiction proves the inequality.",
