          "claim": "Put $\\Phi=x_1+i\\psi$. By [F1] and $|d\\psi|_{g_0}=1$,\n$$g(d\\Phi,d\\Phi)=1+i^2|d\\psi|_{g_0}^2=0.$$\nDirect conjugation gives\n$$(-\\Delta_g+q)(e^{-\\tau\\Phi}a) =e^{-\\tau\\Phi}\\left[\\tau^2g(d\\Phi,d\\Phi)a+ \\tau\\left(2g(\\nabla_g\\Phi,\\nabla_ga)+(\\Delta_g\\Phi)a\\right) +(-\\Delta_g+q)a\\right].$$\nThe $\\tau^2$ term vanishes by the eikonal equality, and the coefficient of $\\tau$ is exactly the transport equation in the statement. Hence the residual is $e^{-\\tau\\Phi}(-\\Delta_g+q)a$.",
