          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $(M,g)$ be a compact smooth Riemannian domain with smooth boundary and no orientability assumption, let $q\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$, and suppose the only $w\\in H_0^1(M)$ satisfying $(-\\Delta_g+q)w=0$ weakly is $w=0$. For every $F\\in L^2(M)$ and $f\\in H^{1/2}(\\partial M)$ there is a unique weak solution $u\\in H^1(M)$ of $(-\\Delta_g+q)u=F$ with trace $f$. If $f=0$, $F\\in H^m(M)$ and $m\\geq0$ is an integer, then $u\\in H^{m+2}(M)$ and $\\|u\\|_{H^{m+2}}\\leq C_m\\|F\\|_{H^m}$. If $F$ and $f$ are smooth, this solution belongs to $H^m(M)$ for every integer $m\\geq0$.",
