          "source": "def-riemannian-volume-density",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Riemannian volume density** is $\\mu_g=\\sqrt{\\det G_x}\\,|dx^1\\cdots dx^n|$ in coordinates.\n\nThe matrix is that of [[prop-coordinate-criterion-for-a-riemannian-metric]], so its determinant is positive and smooth. The density frames and their absolute-Jacobian law are [[def-density-bundle-and-smooth-density]]. In dimension zero take the empty determinant to be one, giving weight one at every point, independently of orientation. The compatibility of these local formulas is proved in [[lem-the-riemannian-volume-density-is-coordinate-independent]].",
