    "ex-ip-transversally-anisotropic-product-with-simple-transversal": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-ip-transversally-anisotropic-product-domain",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A transversally anisotropic product domain of dimension $n\\geq3$ is a compact connected smooth $n$-dimensional Riemannian domain $(M,g)$ with smooth boundary, together with a compact connected smooth $(n-1)$-dimensional Riemannian manifold with boundary $(M_0,g_0)$ and an isometric embedding of $(M,g)$ as a smooth domain compactly contained in $(\\mathbb R\\times M_0^\\circ,dx_1^2\\oplus g_0)$. The coordinate $x_1$ on $\\mathbb R$ is the distinguished Euclidean coordinate; $M_0$ is the transversal manifold. All Laplacians use $\\Delta_g=\\operatorname{div}_g\\nabla_g$. Neither $M$ nor $M_0$ is assumed orientable. A positive smooth conformal factor is not included in this definition; claims using a conformally related metric must state and prove the required conformal transformation separately.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-ip-simple-surface-and-geodesic-xray-transform",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $(M,g)$ be a compact, connected, nonempty smooth two-dimensional Riemannian manifold with smooth boundary. For $x\\in\\partial M$, let $\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}(x)$ be the outward unit normal. The boundary is **strictly convex** if\n$$\ng(\\nabla_w\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}},w)>0\n$$\nfor every $x\\in\\partial M$ and every nonzero $w\\in T_x\\partial M$. A **Jacobi field** along a unit-speed geodesic $\\gamma$ is a smooth vector field $J$ along $\\gamma$ satisfying\n$$\nD_t^2J+R(J,\\dot\\gamma)\\dot\\gamma=0,\n$$\nwhere $R(X,Y)Z=\\nabla_X\\nabla_YZ-\\nabla_Y\\nabla_XZ-\\nabla_{[X,Y]}Z$. The manifold has **no conjugate points** if, on every unit-speed geodesic segment $\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$, a Jacobi field with $J(a)=J(b)=0$ must be identically zero. It is **nontrapping** if every maximal unit-speed geodesic starting in $M^\\circ$ reaches $\\partial M$ in finite forward and backward time. The pair $(M,g)$ is a **simple surface** if its boundary is strictly convex, it has no conjugate points, and it is nontrapping.\n\nThe unit tangent bundle is $SM=\\{(x,v):x\\in M,\\ v\\in T_xM,\\ g_x(v,v)=1\\}$. Write $\\nu_{\\mathrm{in}}=-\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}$ and\n$$\n\\partial_+SM=\\{(x,v)\\in SM:x\\in\\partial M,\\ g_x(v,\\nu_{\\mathrm{in}})>0\\}\n$$\nfor inward-pointing unit boundary vectors. For $(x,v)\\in\\partial_+SM$, let $\\gamma_{x,v}$ be the unit-speed geodesic with $\\gamma_{x,v}(0)=x$ and $\\dot\\gamma_{x,v}(0)=v$, and let $\\tau_+(x,v)$ be its first positive exit time from $M$. For $f\\in C^\\infty(M)$, its scalar **geodesic X-ray transform** is the function on $\\partial_+SM$ defined by\n$$\nI_0f(x,v)=\\int_0^{\\tau_+(x,v)} f(\\gamma_{x,v}(t))\\,dt.\n$$\nThe geodesic equation is interpreted up to first boundary exit; local smooth extensions of the metric are used only to solve the coordinate ODE at boundary initial data.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-ip-2d-simple-surface-xray-injectivity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(M,g)$ be a compact, connected, nonempty smooth Riemannian surface with smooth boundary. Write $\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}}$ for its outward unit normal and use the curvature convention $R(A,B)C=\\nabla_A\\nabla_BC-\\nabla_B\\nabla_AC-\\nabla_{[A,B]}C$. Write $D_tJ=\\nabla_{\\dot\\gamma}J$; a Jacobi field along a unit-speed geodesic $\\gamma$ is a smooth field $J$ satisfying $D_t^2J+R(J,\\dot\\gamma)\\dot\\gamma=0$. Assume $g(\\nabla_w\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}},w)>0$ for every nonzero boundary-tangent vector $w$, no nonzero Jacobi field on any positive-length unit-speed geodesic segment vanishes at both endpoints, and every maximal unit-speed geodesic starting in $M^\\circ$ reaches $\\partial M$ in finite forward and backward time. Set $SM=\\{(x,v):x\\in M,\\ g_x(v,v)=1\\}$ and $\\partial_+SM=\\{(x,v)\\in SM:x\\in\\partial M,\\ g_x(v,-\\nu_{\\mathrm{out}})>0\\}$. For a real-valued $f\\in C_c^\\infty(M^\\circ,\\mathbb R)$ and $(x,v)\\in\\partial_+SM$, let $\\gamma_{x,v}$ be the unit-speed geodesic with initial data $(x,v)$, let $\\tau_+(x,v)$ be its first positive boundary-exit time, and define\n$$\nI_0f(x,v)=\\int_0^{\\tau_+(x,v)} f(\\gamma_{x,v}(t))\\,dt.\n$$\nThen $I_0f=0$ on $\\partial_+SM$ implies $f=0$ on $M$. No orientability assumption on $M$ is required.",
