          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The critical points are isolated in the compact one-dimensional skeleton and absent from the tangle boundary, so there are finitely many critical points and critical values. On every open interval between consecutive critical values or boundary levels, the inverse image is a finite union of arcs on which $t$ is a local diffeomorphism. Thus the number of branches, and the finite set of allowed pairs at a level, are constant on each such interval.",
