          "claim": "Fix $i<j<k$ and put $a=t_{ij}$, $b=t_{ik}$, $c=t_{jk}$, $x=\\alpha_{ij}$, $y=\\alpha_{ik}$, and $z=\\alpha_{jk}$. The tangled 4T relation on these three strands is exactly the pair of infinitesimal braid relations $[a,b+c]=0$ and $[b,a+c]=0$. The contribution of this triple is $[a,b]x\\wedge y+[a,c]x\\wedge z+[b,c]y\\wedge z$. The infinitesimal braid relations in [F1] give $[a,c]=-[a,b]$ and $[b,c]=[a,b]$, so this is $[a,b](x\\wedge y-x\\wedge z+y\\wedge z)$. With $u=z_i-z_j$ and $v=z_j-z_k$, we have $x=du/u$, $z=dv/v$, and $y=d(u+v)/(u+v)$. Direct expansion gives $x\\wedge z+z\\wedge y+y\\wedge x=(1/(uv)-1/(v(u+v))-1/(u(u+v)))du\\wedge dv=0$, which is equivalent to $x\\wedge y-x\\wedge z+y\\wedge z=0$. Thus every triple contribution vanishes.",
