        {
          "id": "step-5-1",
          "claim": "Fix a smooth path $\\gamma$ and let $U(t)$ solve $\\dot U=A_tU$, $U(0)=1$, where $A_t=\\Omega_q(\\dot\\gamma(t))$. In each degree this is a finite linear ODE system, solved recursively by the iterated-integral formula. For a homotopy $\\gamma(s,t)$ with fixed endpoints, set $A_s=\\Omega_q(\\partial_s\\gamma)$ and $W=U^{-1}(\\partial_sU-A_sU)$. Differentiating and using $\\partial_tU=A_tU$ gives $\\partial_tW=U^{-1}(\\partial_sA_t-\\partial_tA_s+[A_t,A_s])U$. The coefficient in parentheses is the evaluation of the flatness expression from step 4.1, so it is zero. Since the initial endpoint is fixed, $W(s,0)=0$ and hence $W(s,t)=0$; at the fixed terminal endpoint $A_s=0$, so $\\partial_sU(s,1)=0$. The holonomy is therefore constant throughout the homotopy.",
