          "id": "step-6-1",
          "claim": "The KZ form is unchanged by relabeling the strands, since its sum runs over every unordered pair; endpoint strand permutations therefore act on holonomy by the same permutation of the $t_{ij}$. For $|i-j|\\ge2$, the paths for $\\sigma_i$ and $\\sigma_j$ lie in disjoint two-point disks, so exchanging their time intervals is a fixed-endpoint homotopy and step 5.1 gives $\\sigma_i\\sigma_j=\\sigma_j\\sigma_i$. For three adjacent points, start at $(-1,0,1)$ and follow the configuration path $(-e^{\\pi it},0,e^{\\pi it})$, $0\\le t\\le1$. Its endpoints agree as unordered configurations with the three points reversed, and its pairwise distances stay bounded below by $1$. At $t=1/2$ the three real projections coincide. Small perturbations of the trajectories therefore remain collision-free and can separate the three projected crossing times in either of the two orders; both perturbed paths are homotopic to this rigid half-turn and give respectively $\\sigma_i\\sigma_{i+1}\\sigma_i$ and $\\sigma_{i+1}\\sigma_i\\sigma_{i+1}$. By step 5.1 their transports agree.",
