          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Near a nondegenerate maximum, use the Morse coordinate $s=\\sqrt{t_c-t}$ from [F2]. The two local branch functions satisfy $z_+(s)=z_c+a s+O(s^2)$ and $z_-(s)=z_c-a s+O(s^2)$ for some $a\\ne0$; this follows because the tangle or knot immersion has nonzero tangent and $dt/ds=0$ at the critical point, so its tangent there is horizontal. Hence $|z_+(s)-z_-(s)|\\asymp s$ and the short logarithmic form has absolute size at most $C\\,ds/s$. A minimum has the same estimate after reversing $t$.",
