          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every integer $q\\ge2$, let $\\operatorname{Conf}_q(\\mathbb C)$ be the space of ordered $q$-tuples of pairwise distinct complex points, and let $\\widehat{\\mathcal A}_{\\mathbb C}(q)$ and $t_{ij}$ be as defined for parenthesized braids. Write $\\sigma_i$ for the positive geometric half twist interchanging adjacent strands $i$ and $i+1$ in a disk containing no other strand. The Knizhnik–Zamolodchikov form\n$$\\Omega_q=\\frac1{2\\pi i}\\sum_{1\\le i<j\\le q}t_{ij}\\,d\\log(z_i-z_j)$$\nsatisfies $d\\Omega_q=0$ and $\\Omega_q\\wedge\\Omega_q=0$. Consequently the degreewise iterated-integral holonomy depends only on the homotopy class of a path with fixed endpoints. On geometric braids this holonomy respects the distant commutation relations $\\sigma_i\\sigma_j=\\sigma_j\\sigma_i$ for $|i-j|\\ge2$ and the adjacent braid relations $\\sigma_i\\sigma_{i+1}\\sigma_i=\\sigma_{i+1}\\sigma_i\\sigma_{i+1}$.",
