          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "An orientation-preserving reparametrization of $K$ preserves the cyclic order of every chord endpoint, the set of points at each height, the down-endpoint sign, and the pulled-back differential form. Hence every degree coefficient of $Z(K)$ is unchanged, and the reparametrization preserves $r(K)$. A positive affine change $t\\mapsto at+b$ of the height also preserves each coefficient: substitute $u_j=at_j+b$ in the ordered level integrals; the branch pairings and logarithmic forms correspond term by term. Thus $I(K)$ is unchanged under both operations.",
