          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-kontsevich-integral-is-universal",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice. Let $\\mathcal V_n^{\\mathbb C}$ be the $\\mathbb C$-vector space of ambient-isotopy invariants of oriented knots with values in $\\mathbb C$ and type at most $n$, where type at most $n$ means that the alternating resolution sum on every $(n+1)$-singular knot is zero; set $\\mathcal V_{-1}^{\\mathbb C}=0$. Let $\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{un}}$ be the rational vector space on degree-$n$ circle chord diagrams modulo 4T and 1T; a weight system is a $\\mathbb Q$-linear functional on this space. For an $n$-singular knot with chord diagram $D$, define $\\sigma_n([V])(D)$ to be the $n$-fold alternating resolution sum of $V$ on that knot. Let $I_{\\le n}(K)=\\sum_{j=0}^{n}I_j(K)$ be the degree-$n$ truncation of the normalized unframed Kontsevich series. The degree-$n$ symbol map\n$$\n\\sigma_n:\\mathcal V_n^{\\mathbb C}/\\mathcal V_{n-1}^{\\mathbb C}\\longrightarrow \\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb Q}(\\mathcal A_n^{\\mathrm{un}},\\mathbb C)\n$$\nis surjective. In particular, every rational weight system has a complex-valued finite-type lift; no rationality claim is made about that lift or about the coefficients of $I(K)$. Moreover, for every $n$ and every $V\\in\\mathcal V_n^{\\mathbb C}$ there is a complex-linear functional $\\Lambda_V$ on $\\bigoplus_{j=0}^{n}(\\mathcal A_j^{\\mathrm{un}}\\otimes_{\\mathbb Q}\\mathbb C)$ whose degree-$n$ restriction is the degree-$n$ symbol of $V$ and such that\n$$\nV(K)=\\Lambda_V(I_{\\le n}(K))\n$$\nfor every oriented knot type $K$. This recovery statement does not imply that distinct knot types have distinct Kontsevich series.",
