      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-knot-floer-cobordism-map",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $(W,\\Sigma,\\mathcal A)$ be a decorated knot cobordism from $(Y_0,K_0)$ to $(Y_1,K_1)$, and fix $\\mathfrak s\\in\\operatorname{Spin}^c(W)$. Choose a parametrized Kirby decomposition of $W$, together with admissible Heegaard data and regular almost-complex structures for its elementary pieces. Intermediate pieces may contain links with several components or more than one pair of basepoints. Use the colored multipointed modules with $g+n-1$ attaching curves in $\\operatorname{Sym}^{g+n-1}(S)$, and specialize all $w$-colors to $U$ and all $z$-colors to $V$; the displayed doubly pointed formula is the $n=1$ case. For a piece represented by a subordinate Heegaard triple $(S,\\boldsymbol\\alpha,\\boldsymbol\\beta,\\boldsymbol\\gamma,w,z)$, its triangle-count map has the form\n$$\n\\mathbf x\\longmapsto \\sum_{\\mathbf y}\\ \\sum_{\\substack{\\phi\\in\\pi_2(\\mathbf x,\\Theta^+_{\\boldsymbol\\beta\\boldsymbol\\gamma},\\mathbf y)\\\\ \\mu(\\phi)=0,\\ \\mathfrak s(\\phi)=\\mathfrak s}} \\#_2\\bigl(\\mathcal M(\\phi)\\bigr)U^{n_w(\\phi)}V^{n_z(\\phi)}\\mathbf y,\n$$\nwhere $\\Theta^+_{\\boldsymbol\\beta\\boldsymbol\\gamma}$ denotes a chosen cycle representative of the distinguished top-degree homology class of the appropriate standard auxiliary Heegaard pair, $\\mathfrak s(\\phi)$ is the Spin-c structure determined by the triangle class, and the other symbols and coefficient ring are as in the two-color target definition. For a chosen auxiliary cycle with finite support $\\Theta=\\sum_j p_j\\theta_j$, with $p_j\\in\\mathbb F_2[U,V]$ and basis generators $\\theta_j$, interpret the displayed formula by $\\mathbb F_2[U,V]$-linearity as $\\sum_j p_j F(\\mathbf x,\\theta_j)$ (or $\\sum_j p_j F(\\theta_j,\\mathbf x)$ for the alpha-triple convention). The elementary 2-handle maps and band maps are triangle-count maps; the 0-, 1-, 3-, and 4-handle maps use the corresponding stabilization or destabilization maps; cylindrical changes of the dividing set use basepoint and quasi-stabilization maps. Compose the elementary maps in the chosen decomposition to obtain a representative\n$$\n\\widetilde F_{W,\\Sigma,\\mathcal A,\\mathfrak s,\\mathcal K}: CFL^-_{UV}(Y_0,K_0,\\mathfrak s|_{Y_0})\\longrightarrow CFL^-_{UV}(Y_1,K_1,\\mathfrak s|_{Y_1}).\n$$\nThe subscript $\\mathcal K$ records the chosen decomposition and auxiliary data. This is one map for one Spin-c structure; maps for different Spin-c structures are not summed unless a sum is explicitly specified. Independence from $\\mathcal K$, regular data, and parametrization is a separate naturality assertion.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.3"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
