        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "For different endpoint diagrams first use [F1]'s canonical transition chain-homotopy equivalences to compare maps on the same chosen endpoint representatives. Theorem A then gives a filtered equivariant chain homotopy for any two admitted decompositions and regular auxiliary choices. The source's fourteen Cerf moves include the band, basepoint and quasi-stabilization relations; §12.5 additionally handles components missing one or both ends. Boundary-fixed ambient isotopy preserves the given decorations and induces precisely the required diffeomorphism of decorated cobordisms, so it is covered by the same theorem.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
