            "step 1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-4",
          "claim": "Finally $H^2(S^3\\times[0,1];\\mathbb Z)=0$ and the product is spin. Its nonempty Spin-c torsor therefore consists of one element. In the stated product case the extension set has precisely that element and the law reduces to ordinary composition up to filtered equivariant chain homotopy. The argument imports the established naturality/composition theorems, not an unproved assertion that the local triangle identity checks all movies.",
