        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-carter-saito-movie-move-equivalence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice. Let $\\Sigma_0,\\Sigma_1\\subset S^3\\times[0,1]$ be compact smooth properly embedded oriented surfaces from fixed oriented knots $K_0$ to $K_1$, with the same boundary parametrizations and product collars. Suppose their generic movies represent ambient isotopic cobordisms by an isotopy fixed on those collars. Then one movie can be changed to the other by a finite sequence of the fifteen Carter–Saito movie moves, sweep-around moves, and interchanges of two disjoint elementary movie events (including disjoint critical points of the surface-height function). A sweep-around moves a closing arc of a one-interval tangle over the tangle to its other side and back underneath, or reverses that movie; geometrically it is a local sheet passage through the missing vertical arc in a spatial chart $S^3\\setminus\\{\\infty\\}$. Every intermediate movie represents a generic surface cobordism with the same fixed boundary data.",
