        {
          "id": "step-4-2",
          "claim": "**An explicit finite verification model.** The next matrices are defined independently in the local category just constructed. Their equations can be checked faithfully after adjoining the distinct pigments. Write a three-strand boundary coloring as $v\\in\\{0,1\\}^3$, where the two pigment values are $0,1$ after scaling their difference. A word in $A=A_1$ and $C=A_2$ has basis the paths $(v_0,\\ldots,v_m)$ such that at its $i$th-letter step the relevant two colors are distinct and $v_j$ is either $v_{j-1}$ or their interchange. With $\\delta_i(v)=v_i-v_{i+1}$, the elementary operators have the following complete rules: $\\eta_i:I\\to A_i$ inserts the unchanged color path with coefficient $\\delta_i(v)$; $\\varepsilon_i:A_i\\to I$ deletes a step only when its two endpoints agree, with coefficient $1$; $\\Delta_i:A_i\\to A_iA_i$ sums all allowed middle color orders with coefficient $1$; and $m_i:A_iA_i\\to A_i$ removes the middle color $u$ with coefficient $1/\\delta_i(u)$. Indeed the circle birth is the sum of its two idempotents and its cap has values $\\beta_i$; zip followed by unzip has the values $0,d,-d,0$ on equal/equal, first/second, second/first, and second/second colors. Normalizing unzip to $1$ gives exactly these rules. The unit and counit identities determine the displayed digon coefficients as well: $\\delta_i(u)\\beta_i=1$. All four are actual integral foams; only their color coordinates use inverses of $d$. Put $U_i=\\Delta_i\\eta_i$ and $V_i=\\varepsilon_i m_i$. Faithfulness of this color test follows from the defining radical: a morphism whose every pigment coefficient is zero pairs to zero with every closure. Torsion-freeness from step 3.1 then reflects equality back before localization.",
