        {
          "id": "step-5-1",
          "claim": "**Four complete third-move matrices.** Products below compose rightmost first, juxtaposed operators act on the indicated tensor factors, and omitted entries are zero. At each three-crossing cube order vertices by masks $(0,1,2,4,3,5,6,7)$; hence its four consecutive terms have sizes $1,3,3,1$. A positive factor is $A_i\\to I$ in degrees $(-1,0)$ and a negative factor is $I\\to A_i$ in degrees $(0,1)$, with the prefix tensor signs. The four source/target sign patterns are $(+++;+++)$, $(--+;+--)$, $(++-;-++)$ and $(---;---)$ on the words $ACA,CAC$. The source and target term lists, respectively, are $(ACA;(CA,AA,AC);(A,C,A);I)$ and $(CAC;(AC,CC,CA);(C,A,C);I)$ in case I; $(A;(AA,CA,I);(ACA,A,C);AC)$ and $(C;(I,CA,CC);(A,C,CAC);AC)$ in case II; $(AC;(C,A,ACA);(I,CA,AA);A)$ and $(AC;(CAC,C,A);(CC,CA,I);C)$ in case III; and $(I;(A,C,A);(AC,AA,CA);ACA)$ and $(I;(C,A,C);(CA,CC,AC);CAC)$ in case IV. Their maps on the four consecutive terms are $0,M_1,M_2,1$ in I, $0,N_1,N_2,1$ in II, $1,P_1,P_2,0$ in III, and $1,Q_1,Q_2,0$ in IV, where $$M_1=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-(1_A\\eta_C)m_A&1_{AC}\\\\-\\Delta_C(1_C\\varepsilon_A)&U_CV_A&0\\\\1_{CA}&-(\\eta_C1_A)m_A&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad M_2=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1_C&0\\\\1_A&0&1_A\\\\0&0&0\\end{pmatrix},$$ $$N_1=\\begin{pmatrix}-V_A&0&1\\\\-(\\eta_C1_A)m_A&1_{CA}&0\\\\U_CV_A&-\\Delta_C(1_C\\varepsilon_A)&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad N_2=\\begin{pmatrix}m_A(1_A\\varepsilon_C1_A)&1_A&0\\\\0&0&1_C\\\\0&0&0\\end{pmatrix},$$ $$P_1=\\begin{pmatrix}-(1_C\\eta_A1_C)\\Delta_C&0&0\\\\1_C&0&0\\\\0&1_A&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad P_2=\\begin{pmatrix}U_C&-\\Delta_C(1_C\\varepsilon_A)&U_CV_A\\\\0&1_{CA}&-(\\eta_C1_A)m_A\\\\1&0&0\\end{pmatrix},$$ and $$Q_1=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1_C&0\\\\1_A&0&0\\\\0&1_C&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad Q_2=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-(\\eta_C1_A)m_A&1_{CA}\\\\-\\Delta_C(\\varepsilon_A1_C)&U_CV_A&-\\Delta_C(1_C\\varepsilon_A)\\\\1_{AC}&0&0\\end{pmatrix}.$$ These are rank-two representatives of the four local slides: the moving strand goes from first top endpoint to third bottom endpoint, so its two crossings are the first two source factors and last two target factors. The remaining third source/first target crossing is the fixed internal crossing, positive in I–II and negative in III–IV. This specifies the physical variants without relying on an unlabelled picture or an omitted six-valent foam.",
