        {
          "id": "step-7-1",
          "claim": "**These are actual local equivalences.** The dotted pairing calculation in step 3.1 and the boundary-crossing inverse equivalences in [F4] identify the full degree-zero endomorphism ring of each local braid complex with $\\mathbb Z$. Let $G$ be any of the known equivalences in [F4], transported through step 4.1, and let $F$ be one of step 5.1's chain maps. Then $G^{-1}F$ is an integer scalar in the homotopy category. To determine that scalar, give all three strands the same pigment. Every state with a thick letter vanishes, and only the parallel term remains, in degree zero. Its coefficient is a homotopy invariant and is multiplicative, since all other states are zero in this channel. The parallel coefficient of an integral equivalence and its inverse multiply to $1$, so each is $\\pm1$; the parallel coefficient of every $F$ above is $1$. Consequently $F=\\pm G$ in the homotopy category and is itself an equivalence. This proves comparison with the fixed local maps without requiring an unverified equality between a cone representative and a chosen parameter value in a published family.",
