          "id": "step-8-1",
          "claim": "**The first and second moves used by the sweep.** In the normalized ordinary Frobenius algebra, let $u$ create the small circle and $e$ cap it. The four relevant kink maps are $u$, $(Y-X)u$, $e$, and $e(Y-X)$, where $X$ is the continuing-arc dot and $Y$ the small-circle dot. Indeed $v-\\Delta=(Y-X)u$ and $w-m=e(Y-X)$: on $1,X$, $v=2Yu$, $\\Delta(1)=1\\otimes X+X\\otimes1$, $\\Delta(X)=X\\otimes X$, and the reverse calculation is the same counit computation. These are precisely [F4]'s two kink retractions. In the auxiliary picture label the two fronts so $R1_+=u$, $R1_-=(Y-X)u$, $R1_+^{-1}=e(Y-X)$ and $R1_-^{-1}=e$; reversing all labels changes no conclusion. Their only nonzero components have external degree zero. For one pair of inverse external crossings, order the middle summands as $I,A_iA_i$. The two physical orders have inclusions $(1,-U_i)^T,(1,U_i)^T$ and projections $(1,V_i),(1,-V_i)$. The unit/counit rules in step 4.2 give the chain-map equations, and $V_iU_i=0$, so their projection-inclusion composites are $1$. Their homotopy equivalences are also supplied by the actual inverse-crossing retractions in [F4], or by the same scalar test as step 7.1. Thus a succession of $n$ such pairs is supported only on palindromic thick/parallel states, preserves external degree, and the two fronts differ on a palindrome with $2k$ thick letters by $(-1)^k$, for either the inclusion or the projection. This is one sign from each double-thick pair; the all-parallel component is always $1$.",
