          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-barnatan-khovanov-cobordism-functoriality-up-to-sign",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice. Let $\\Sigma\\subset S^3\\times[0,1]$ be a compact smooth oriented cobordism from an oriented knot $K_0$ to an oriented knot $K_1$, with fixed product collars and fixed endpoint diagrams. Every generic movie $M$ of $\\Sigma$ defines a map of bidegree $(0,\\chi(\\Sigma))$,\n$$\nKh(M):Kh^{i,j}(K_0)\\longrightarrow Kh^{i,j+\\chi(\\Sigma)}(K_1),\n$$\nwhere $\\chi(\\Sigma)$ is the Euler characteristic of the surface and the integral even Khovanov groups use the normalized crossing shifts. If two such movies represent cobordisms related by an ambient isotopy fixed on the boundary collars, their maps differ by multiplication by a single overall sign, independent of the input class. The resulting assignment is a functor after each morphism group is quotiented by the relation identifying a map with its negative; before that quotient the sign is not canonical.",
