          "claim": "Write $z=Y-Am_0$ and $e=Y-A\\theta=\\eta$. By [F4], the log likelihood ratio in [F1] is $\\log\\frac{p(Y\\mid\\theta)}{p_Y(Y)}=\\frac12\\log\\frac{\\det S}{\\det\\Gamma}-\\frac12e^T\\Gamma^{-1}e+\\frac12z^TS^{-1}z$. The two quadratic terms have finite expectations: expanding each finite sum and using $\\mathbb E[ee^T]=\\Gamma$ and $\\mathbb E[zz^T]=S$ gives $\\mathbb E[e^T\\Gamma^{-1}e]=\\operatorname{tr}(\\Gamma^{-1}\\Gamma)=m$ and $\\mathbb E[z^TS^{-1}z]=\\operatorname{tr}(S^{-1}S)=m$. Their expectations cancel, so [F1] yields $\\operatorname{EIG}=\\frac12\\log(\\det S/\\det\\Gamma)$.",
