          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice for the library's Kullback–Leibler divergence convention. For a design $d$ in a design-indexed dominated inverse experiment, let $G_d=\\{y:0<p_d(y)<\\infty\\}$ be its positive finite evidence fibers. The **expected information gain** is\n$$\\operatorname{EIG}(d):=\\int_{G_d}D(\\mu_d^y\\|\\mu_0)\\,p_d(y)\\,\\nu(dy)\\in[0,+\\infty],$$\nwhere the integrand is defined to be zero outside $G_d$. Here $D(P\\|Q)$ is the directional Kullback–Leibler divergence of probability measures, with natural logarithms.",
