          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $n,m\\ge1$, let $m_0\\in\\mathbb R^n$, let $C\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$ be symmetric positive semidefinite, let $A\\in\\mathbb R^{m\\times n}$, and let $\\Gamma\\in\\mathbb R^{m\\times m}$ be symmetric positive definite. Suppose $\\theta\\sim N_n(m_0,C)$ and $\\eta\\sim N_m(0,\\Gamma)$ are independent, and observe $Y=A\\theta+\\eta$. With $S=ACA^T+\\Gamma$, the expected information gain of this experiment is\n$$\\operatorname{EIG}=\\frac12\\log\\det\\!\\left(I_m+\\Gamma^{-1/2}ACA^T\\Gamma^{-1/2}\\right).$$\nHere $\\Gamma^{-1/2}$ is the inverse of the unique symmetric positive-definite square root of $\\Gamma$, and $\\log$ is the natural logarithm. The matrix inside the log determinant is positive definite. This formula permits singular $C$ and never uses differential entropy of $\\theta$; the mean $m_0$ cancels. Noise depending on $\\theta$ is outside the hypotheses and need not satisfy the formula.",
