          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal T)$ be a topological space (Topology on a set, open and closed sets, clopen sets, the closed-set axiomatisation, and the coarser/finer comparison). The\n**Borel sigma-algebra of $X$** is the sigma-algebra generated by its open sets:\n\n$$\\mathcal B(X):=\\sigma_X(\\mathcal T).$$\n\nIts members are the **Borel subsets** of $X$. The generated sigma-algebra exists\nand is minimal by Nonempty intersections of sigma-algebras are sigma-algebras, so the generated sigma-algebra exists and is minimal.",
