          "quote": "Let $X$ be a specified real separable Banach or Hilbert parameter space with metric $d_X(x,x')=\\|x-x'\\|_X$ and its norm topology. Let $(Y,d_Y)$ be a metric data space equipped with a sigma-algebra $\\Sigma_Y$, let $U\\subseteq X$ be a nonempty admissible truth set, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be a forward map. Choose a Borel set $D\\in\\mathcal B(X)$ with $D\\subseteq U$ such that the restriction $G:=F|_D:D\\to Y$ is measurable for the trace Borel sigma-algebra $\\mathcal B(D):=\\{D\\cap A:A\\in\\mathcal B(X)\\}$. A prior on this forward domain is a Borel probability measure $\\mu$ on $X$ such that $\\mu(D)=1$. Its restriction $\\mu|_D$, defined by $\\mu|_D(A)=\\mu(A)$ for $A\\in\\mathcal B(D)$, is then a probability measure on $D$, and the induced data law is $G_\\#(\\mu|_D)$, defined by $G_\\#(\\mu|_D)(E)=(\\mu|_D)(G^{-1}(E))$ for $E\\in\\Sigma_Y$. A Borel probability on $X$ with $\\mu(D)<1$ is not a prior on this declared forward domain.",
