      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For each $m\\in\\mathbb N$, the initial set $E_m=\\{0,1,\\ldots,m\\}$ has counting measure $m+1<\\infty$ by [F1] and [F2], and $\\bigcup_mE_m=\\mathbb N$. Thus $\\mu$ is sigma-finite by [F3]. By [F16], $\\mathbb N$ is infinite, so [F1] gives $\\mu(\\mathbb N)=+\\infty$.",
