          "id": "derive-3.1",
          "claim": "By step 1.1, $R$ is continuous on $(0,b_1^{-1})$. Given $r^2\\in(0,b_1^{-1})$, steps 2.1 and 2.2 let us choose $0<A_-<A_+<b_1^{-1}$ with $R(A_-)<r^2$ and $R(A_+)=b_1^{-1}$. Apply [F2] to the restriction of $R$ to $[A_-,A_+]$ to obtain $A$ with $R(A)=r^2$. Set $z_0^2=r^2/N(A)>0$ and define $\\widetilde\\eta_j^2=z_0^2\\sigma_j^2(1-Ab_j)_+$. Its support is the finite active set, and $$\\sum_j\\sigma_j^2\\widetilde\\eta_j^2=z_0^2N(A)=r^2,\\qquad \\sum_ja_j^2\\sigma_j^2\\widetilde\\eta_j^2=z_0^2D(A)=\\frac{r^2D(A)}{N(A)}=1.$$ Taking $r_0=b_1^{-1/2}$ proves the assertion and, by [F1], the profile belongs to $\\Theta_2(r)$.",
