          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC and let $G\\sim N(0,\\sigma^2)$ for $\\sigma\\ge0$. Then $\\mathbb E[G^2]=\\sigma^2$ and $\\mathbb E[G^4]=3\\sigma^4$; in particular the fourth moment is finite. For independent centered normal coordinates $G_j\\sim N(0,\\sigma_j^2)$, every finite linear combination of the variables $G_j^2$ has finite second moment.",
