          "source": "lem-ip-weighted-chi-square-triangular-array-limit",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. For each $n$, let $G_{n,1},\\ldots,G_{n,m_n}$ be independent standard normal random variables, and let $w_{n,j}\\ge0$ satisfy $2\\sum_{j=1}^{m_n}w_{n,j}^2=1$. If $\\max_{1\\le j\\le m_n}w_{n,j}\\to0$, then\n$$T_n=\\sum_{j=1}^{m_n}w_{n,j}(G_{n,j}^2-1)$$\nhas mean zero and variance one for every $n$ and converges in distribution to $N(0,1)$.",
