          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-slutsky-for-real-random-variables",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X_n)$ and $(Y_n)$ be real random variables on one probability space, and let $X$ be a real random variable (possibly on another space). If $X_n\\Rightarrow X$ and $Y_n\\to c$ in probability for $c\\in\\mathbb R$, then $X_n+Y_n\\Rightarrow X+c$ and $X_nY_n\\Rightarrow cX$. If $c\\ne0$, define $Q_n=X_n/Y_n$ on $\\{Y_n\\ne0\\}$ and give $Q_n$ any fixed value on $\\{Y_n=0\\}$. Then $Q_n\\Rightarrow X/c$.",
