          "source": "thm-portmanteau-theorem",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For Borel probabilities $\\mu_n,\\mu$ on a metric space S, the following are equivalent: (i) $\\mu_n\\Rightarrow\\mu$; (ii) integrals converge for all bounded uniformly continuous real tests; (iii) $\\limsup_n\\mu_n(F)\\le\\mu(F)$ for every closed F; (iv) $\\liminf_n\\mu_n(G)\\ge\\mu(G)$ for every open G; (v) $\\mu_n(A)\\to\\mu(A)$ for every Borel A with $\\mu(\\partial A)=0$.",
