    "lem-ip-tv-l2-functional-properties": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-ip-tv-functional-on-l2-distributional-variation",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ be open and let $X=L^2(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$. Every $u\\in X$ is integrable on compact subsets by Cauchy\u2013Schwarz. Define its extended distributional total variation by\n$$TV_2(u;\\Omega):=\\sup\\left\\{\\int_\\Omega u\\,\\operatorname{div}\\varphi\\,dx:\\ \\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R^2),\\ \\sup_{x\\in\\Omega}|\\varphi(x)|\\le1\\right\\}\\in[0,+\\infty],$$\nwhere $C_c^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R^2)$ denotes smooth compactly supported vector fields, $|\\cdot|$ is the Euclidean norm, and $\\operatorname{div}\\varphi=\\partial_1\\varphi_1+\\partial_2\\varphi_2$. This definition treats $L^2$ functions as almost-everywhere classes and does not require $u\\in L^1(\\Omega)$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-ip-bv-test-field-characterization-and-lsc",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every open $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ and real-valued $u\\in BV(\\Omega)$, $$TV(u;\\Omega)=\\sup\\left\\{\\int_\\Omega u\\,\\operatorname{div}\\varphi\\,dx:\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R^n),\\ |\\varphi(x)|\\le1\\right\\}.$$ If $u_k,u\\in BV(\\Omega)$ are real-valued and $u_k\\to u$ in $L^1(\\Omega)$, then $TV(u;\\Omega)\\le\\liminf_kTV(u_k;\\Omega)$. In addition, assuming Countable Choice, for any real-valued $u\\in L^1(\\Omega)$ the displayed supremum is finite if and only if $u\\in BV(\\Omega)$, with equality to $TV(u;\\Omega)$; under the same assumption, an $L^1$ limit of real-valued BV functions with bounded liminf total variation belongs to $BV(\\Omega)$ and satisfies the same lower-semicontinuity inequality.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For all vectors $x,y$ in a real or complex inner-product space,\n\n$$|\\langle x,y\\rangle|\\le\\|x\\|\\,\\|y\\| ,$$\n\nwith equality if and only if $x$ and $y$ are linearly dependent.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "derive-1-1",
          "claim": "The zero function has $TV_2(0;\\Omega)=0$, so the functional is proper; its defining test class is symmetric under $\\varphi\\mapsto-\\varphi$, hence its supremum is nonnegative. For $\\lambda>0$, linearity of every test integral gives $TV_2(\\lambda u;\\Omega)=\\lambda TV_2(u;\\Omega)$, and the equality also holds for $\\lambda=0$. For $\\theta\\in[0,1]$, every admissible field gives $\\int(\\theta u+(1-\\theta)v)\\operatorname{div}\\varphi\\le\\theta TV_2(u;\\Omega)+(1-\\theta)TV_2(v;\\Omega)$; taking the supremum proves convexity, with the extended-real cases automatic.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "derive-2-1",
          "claim": "By [F3], every fixed test integral is a continuous linear functional on $L^2$. For each real $a$, the sublevel set $\\{u:TV_2(u;\\Omega)\\le a\\}$ is the intersection, over all admissible $\\varphi$, of the closed half-spaces $\\{u:\\int u\\operatorname{div}\\varphi\\le a\\}$; hence it is closed and $TV_2$ is lower semicontinuous. If $u\\in BV(\\Omega)\\cap L^2(\\Omega)$, [F1] and [F2] give $TV_2(u;\\Omega)=TV(u;\\Omega)$.",
          "step": "2.1",
