          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^n$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain, meaning a bounded open set whose boundary has a finite cover by Lipschitz graph neighborhoods with $\\Omega$ on one side of each graph. The zero-extension map is bounded from $BV(\\Omega)$ to $BV(\\mathbb R^n)$, with support in $\\overline\\Omega$, and there is a finite $C_\\Omega$ such that $$\\|\\widetilde u\\|_{L^1(\\mathbb R^n)}+TV(\\widetilde u;\\mathbb R^n)\\le C_\\Omega\\bigl(\\|u\\|_{L^1(\\Omega)}+TV(u;\\Omega)\\bigr)$$ for every $u\\in BV(\\Omega)$. For every $v\\in BV(\\mathbb R^n)$ and $h\\in\\mathbb R^n$, $$\\|v(\\cdot+h)-v\\|_{L^1(\\mathbb R^n)}\\le |h|TV(v;\\mathbb R^n).$$",
