          "claim": "By [F2], for each real-valued $u$ the positive and negative level sets use $\\{u>t\\}$ for $t>0$ and $\\{u<t\\}$ for $t<0$. They satisfy the pointwise layer-cake identity $$|u(x)-u_0(x)|=\\int_0^\\infty|\\mathbf1_{\\{u>t\\}}-\\mathbf1_{\\{u_0>t\\}}|\\,dt+\\int_{-\\infty}^0|\\mathbf1_{\\{u<t\\}}-\\mathbf1_{\\{u_0<t\\}}|\\,dt.$$ Integrating and applying [F3] gives $$\\|u_n-u_0\\|_1=\\int_0^\\infty|E_n^+(t)\\mathbin\\triangle E_0^+(t)|\\,dt+\\int_{-\\infty}^0|E_n^-(t)\\mathbin\\triangle E_0^-(t)|\\,dt.$$ The right side tends to zero by step 1.1.",
