          "source": "lem-the-laurent-polynomial-ring-is-noetherian-and-a-unique-factorisation-domain",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The Laurent polynomial ring $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t^{\\pm1}]$ of\n[[def-the-laurent-polynomial-ring]] is Noetherian, hence every ideal of\n$\\Lambda$ is finitely generated, and $\\Lambda$ is a unique factorisation\ndomain; its units are $\\pm t^k$, $k\\in\\mathbb Z$, and $t$ is prime in $\\mathbb Z[t]$ but becomes a unit in $\\Lambda$.",
