          "source": "cor-finite-variable-polynomial-ring-noetherian",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring. Then the iterated polynomial ring\n$R[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]$ of [[def-multivariate-polynomial-ring-by-iteration]] is\nNoetherian for every $n\\in\\mathbb N$.\n\nThe index starts at $0$, where the published definition sets\n$R[x_1,\\ldots,x_0]=R$ and the assertion is the hypothesis itself.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-noetherian-ring-quotients-and-localisations",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring. Then\n\n1. $R/I$ is Noetherian for every ideal $I$ of $R$\n   ([[def-quotient-ring]]), and\n2. $S^{-1}R$ is Noetherian for every multiplicative subset $S\\subseteq R$\n   ([[def-multiplicative-subset-and-localisation]]).\n\nBoth cases include their degenerate instances: $I=R$ makes $R/I$ the zero ring,\nand $0\\in S$ makes $S^{-1}R$ the zero ring, and the zero ring is Noetherian.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-gauss-lemma-over-a-ufd",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a unique factorisation domain and let $K=\\operatorname{Frac}(R)$.\n\n1. If $f,g\\in R[x]$ are primitive, then $fg$ is primitive.\n2. If $p\\in R[x]$ is primitive and has positive degree, then $p$ is irreducible\n   in $R[x]$ if and only if it is irreducible in $K[x]$.\n\nHere a polynomial is **primitive** when its coefficients have no common nonunit\ndivisor.",
