          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For $x=\\Phi_i(v)\\in N(K_i)\\setminus K_i$, write $\\rho=\\lVert v\\rVert>0$ and define\n$$\nF_s(x)=\\Phi_i\\!\\left(\\left((1-s)\\rho+s\\epsilon_i\\right)\\frac{v}{\\rho}\\right),\\qquad 0\\le s\\le1.\n$$\nOn $E_L$ set $F_s(x)=x$. The formula is continuous on each punctured tube and agrees with the identity on its boundary $\\rho=\\epsilon_i$. The products with $I$ of the finitely many punctured closed tubes and $E_L$ form a finite closed cover of $X_L\\times I$; [F5] therefore makes $F:X_L\\times I\\to X_L$ continuous. It starts at the identity, fixes $E_L$ pointwise, and at $s=1$ maps every punctured tube to its boundary, so it is a strong deformation retraction onto $E_L$.",
