          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "A finite CW structure has finitely many open cells. Each open cell is contractible, so its inverse image under a covering is a disjoint union of copies of that cell. The regular deck group $H$ acts freely and transitively on those copies. Choose one lifted copy for each cell; finitely many choices suffice. Every other lift is uniquely a deck translate of the chosen lift, so the lifted cellular chain group in degree $n$ is a free $\\mathbb Z[H]=\\Lambda_r$-module with one basis element per $n$-cell of $E_L$.",
