ism sends each variable to its group-ring basis element; monomials $t_1^{n_1}\\cdots t_r^{n_r}$ correspond bijectively to the basis elements indexed by $n_1[\\mu_1]+\\cdots+n_r[\\mu_r]$. Define the absolute multivariable Alexander module by\n\n$$A_L=H_1(X_L^{\\mathrm{ab}};\\mathbb Z),$$\n\nas a left $\\Lambda_r$-module under the deck action. \u201cAbsolute\u201d means this is ordinary homology of the covering space, not relative homology with respect to a fibre over the basepoint.",
