          "source": "cor-homology-of-spheres",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $n\\ge1$, $\\widetilde H_k(S^n;G)$ is $G$ for $k=n$ and $0$ otherwise.\nFor $S^0$, $\\widetilde H_0(S^0;G)\\cong G$ and all other reduced groups vanish.\nThus $H_0(S^n;G)\\cong G$ for $n\\ge1$, whereas\n$H_0(S^0;G)\\cong G\\oplus G$.",
          "uses": [
