        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "prop-relative-transversality-preserves-a-map-on-a-closed-good-region",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $f:M\\to N$ be smooth and let $Z\\subseteq N$ be a closed embedded\nsubmanifold. Suppose $f$ is already transverse to $Z$ on an open neighbourhood\nof a closed set $A\\subseteq M$. Then in the transversality homotopy theorem one\ncan choose the perturbation family so that the perturbed map and the whole\nhomotopy agree with $f$ on a smaller neighbourhood of $A$.",
