          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-relative-whitney-approximation-for-manifold-valued-maps",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume countable choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $F:M\\to N$ be continuous, let $A\\subseteq M$ be closed, and suppose $F$ is smooth on an open neighbourhood of $A$. Then there exist a smooth map $\\widetilde F:M\\to N$ and an open neighbourhood $W$ of $A$ such that $\\widetilde F=F$ on $W$ and $F$ is homotopic to $\\widetilde F$ by a homotopy fixed on $W$, hence relative to $A$. No compactness of $A$ or its neighbourhood is assumed.",
