al. Apply [F4] on this boundaryless source fixing a neighbourhood of $A$. Restrict the resulting transverse map to $[0,1]\\times S^1_J\\times S^1_K$; its unchanged endpoint restrictions are transverse, and [F4] supplies a compact oriented one-dimensional preimage whose boundary is precisely the endpoint preimages. Thus [F3] applies to the restricted family. The endpoint map at $t=1$ misses $\\Delta$, so its intersection number is zero, the same is true at $t=0$, and hence the final mixed signed sum is zero. Thus both the final linking number and the final meridian coefficient are zero. Since step 1.2 shows their changes agree at every switch, the original $\\lambda$ equals the original coefficient $m$.",
