          "quote": "Assume full AC. Use the canonical geometric Artin half twist in the oriented chart $(x,y,t)$, the canonical crossing sign $\\det_P(v_{\\rm over},v_{\\rm under})$, and the Seifert convention $\\theta(u,v)=\\operatorname{lk}(u^+,v)$. Let $F$ be the oriented braid Seifert surface consisting of two Seifert disks and the three crossing bands of the closure of $\\sigma_1^3$. Label the bands in braid order $e_1,e_2,e_3$, oriented as edges from the first disk to the second. The cycle classes $a=e_1-e_2$ and $b=e_2-e_3$ form an integral basis. Order these two classes as $(u,v)$ so that $u\\cdot_Fv=1$. Then\n$$V_{(u,v)}=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&1\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad V+V^T=\\begin{pmatrix}-2&1\\\\1&-2\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nIn particular the signature is $-2$. The three pair-of-band annuli have core self-pairing $-1$, so they are positive Hopf bands when positive refers to the positively linked oriented boundary, rather than to core self-pairing $+1$.",
