          "claim": "In $E_i\\oplus(-V)$, take the subgroup generated by $(e_j; e_j)$ for the old basis vectors $e_1,\\ldots,e_{2g}$ and by $(b;0)$, where $b$ is the last basis vector of the enlarged lattice. Its rank is $2g+1$, half the total rank. The two displayed enlargement matrices have zero old-to-$b$, $b$-to-old, and $b$-to-$b$ entries. The $V$ and $-V$ blocks cancel on the diagonal generators, while all pairings involving $(b;0)$ vanish. Therefore the form vanishes on this subgroup.",
