          "source": "thm-rational-symmetric-signature-kernel-is-killed-by-four",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W(\\mathbb Q)$ denote the Witt group of nonsingular symmetric bilinear forms over $\\mathbb Q$, with orthogonal sum as addition and metabolic forms set to zero. For every such form $q$, four times its Witt class equals its signature times the class of the four-dimensional identity form. In particular, the kernel of the signature is killed by $4$, including its restriction to the subgroup of even-dimensional classes. The signature image is $\\mathbb Z$ on the full group and $2\\mathbb Z$ on the even-dimensional subgroup.",
          "uses": [
