          "source": "lem-countable-signature-groups-with-exponent-four-kernel-split",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $G$ be a countable abelian group and $s:G\\to\\bigoplus_{n\\ge1}\\mathbb Z$ a homomorphism whose kernel $K$ satisfies $4K=0$. Then $K$ is precisely the torsion subgroup of $G$, and for cardinals $r,u,v\\le\\aleph_0$,\n$$G\\cong\\mathbb Z^{(r)}\\oplus(\\mathbb Z/2\\mathbb Z)^{(u)}\\oplus(\\mathbb Z/4\\mathbb Z)^{(v)}.$$\nIf $G$ contains elements $f_i,p_i,q_i$, indexed by positive integers, such that the $f_i$ are integer-linearly independent, the order-two elements $p_i$ have linearly independent images in $G/2G$, and the $2q_i$ are linearly independent order-two elements with $4q_i=0$, then $r=u=v=\\aleph_0$.",
