          "quote": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,P)$ be a probability space, $\\mathcal G\\subseteq\\mathcal F$ a sub-sigma-algebra, and $X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ integrable. A **conditional-expectation version of $X$ given $\\mathcal G$** is a real, $\\mathcal G$-measurable, integrable function $Y$ such that $\\int_A Y\\,dP=\\int_A X\\,dP$ for every $A\\in\\mathcal G$. No completeness of $\\mathcal G$ is assumed.\n\nExpectation means the integral of Expectation of a nonnegative or integrable random variable. Integrable representatives use The class $L^1(\\mu)$ of integrable functions; quotient notation is introduced after uniqueness.",
