          "source": "alg-kauffman-bracket-state-sum",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The input is a nonempty unoriented regular link diagram $D$: a finite immersed\nplanar projection of one or more circles with finitely many transverse double\npoints, no triple points, and over/under data at each double point. Let $C(D)$\nbe its finite crossing set. At each crossing take the local chart in which the\nover-strand runs southwest to northeast and is drawn continuously over the\nunder-strand, which runs northwest to southeast with a gap at the intersection.\nThe A-smoothing joins the two left endpoints and the two right endpoints, with\nweight $A$; the B-smoothing joins the two top endpoints and the two bottom\nendpoints, with weight $A^{-1}$. These labels are transported with\norientation-preserving changes of local coordinates. Put\n$\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$. The output is the Laurent polynomial $\\langle D\\rangle$.\n\n1. Set an accumulator $p:=0$ in $\\mathbb Z[A^{\\pm1}]$.\n2. For each function $S:C(D)\\to\\{A,B\\}$, smooth every crossing according to\n   $S$, obtaining a crossingless diagram with $|S|$ circles. Count the A- and\n   B-smoothings as $a(S)$ and $b(S)$, and replace\n   $$p\\quad\\text{by}\\quad p+A^{a(S)-b(S)}\\delta^{|S|-1}.$$\n3. Return $p$ after all states have been processed.\n\nThe input is a mathematical diagram object, not a serialized string. The\nprocedure specifies no parsing or malformed-string rejection behavior. Since\nthe diagram has at least one component, every complete smoothing has\n$|S|\\ge1$ and every exponent of $\\delta$ is nonnegative.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-hecke-bracket-trace-dictionary-and-local-descent",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $A$ be an indeterminate, $R_A=\\mathbb Z[A^{\\pm1},(A^{-4}+1)^{-1}]$,\n$q=A^{-2}$, $t=q^2=A^{-4}$, $\\delta=-(q+q^{-1})=-A^2-A^{-2}$, and\n$z_0=-1/(t+1)$. For a nonempty regular diagram $D$, define\n$\\langle D\\rangle$ by summing its crossing smoothings with weights $A$ and\n$A^{-1}$ and the factor $\\delta^{k-1}$ for a state with $k$ circles. Let\n$B_n$ be the $n$-strand Artin braid group with positive geometric generators\n$\\sigma_i$ (label $i$ passes below the midpoint and label $i+1$ passes above),\ndrawn with braid parameter increasing from bottom to top; let\n$e:B_n\\to\\mathbb Z$ be the homomorphism $e(\\sigma_i)=1$. Let $H(n)$ be\nthe type-A Hecke algebra with generators $T_i$, quadratic relation\n$T_i^2=(v-1)T_i+v$, braid relations, and distant commutation; let $\\pi_n$\nsend $\\sigma_i$ to $T_i$. Its normalized Markov trace $\\operatorname{tr}_n$\nsatisfies $\\operatorname{tr}_n(1)=1$, cyclicity, tower restriction, and\n$\\operatorname{tr}_{n+1}(xT_n)=z\\operatorname{tr}_n(x)$. Let\n$\\mathrm{TL}_n$ be the noncrossing pairing algebra with loop value $\\delta$,\nand let $\\operatorname{Tr}_n(D)=\\delta^{c(D)}$ be the unnormalized trace,\nwhere $c(D)$ is the number of circles after joining corresponding top and\nbottom endpoints outside the rectangle; set\n$\\tau_n=\\delta^{-n}\\operatorname{Tr}_n$. For $\\beta\\in B_n$,\n$n\\ge1$, orient its closure in the braid direction. Under the specialization\n$v\\mapsto t$, $z\\mapsto z_0$ of the Hecke tower, one has\n$$\\langle\\widehat\\beta\\rangle =\\delta^{n-1}(-A)^{e(\\beta)}\\operatorname{tr}_n(\\pi_n(\\beta))\\big|_{v=t,\\,z=z_0}.$$\nThe identity gives bracket value $1$ on the one-strand identity closure. Its\npositive and negative Markov stabilizations multiply the raw bracket by\n$-A^3$ and $-A^{-3}$, respectively.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-temperley-lieb-closure-trace-and-partial-trace",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $\\delta\\in R$, and use the noncrossing-pairing diagram category of [[def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category]], with the left factor stacked above the right factor. For a basis diagram $D:n\\to n$, close each top endpoint to the corresponding bottom endpoint outside the rectangle and let $c(D)$ be the number of circles in the resulting finite graph. Define\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_n(D)=\\delta^{c(D)}$$\n\nand extend $R$-linearly to $\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta)$. This is the **unnormalized closure trace**. In particular, $\\operatorname{Tr}_0(1_0)=1$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_n(1_n)=\\delta^n$. No unit or nonzero condition on $\\delta$ is required.\n\nLet $\\cup:0\\to2$ and $\\cap:2\\to0$ be the standard cup and cap in the diagram category. For $n\\ge1$ define the **right partial trace** by\n\n$$\\operatorname{ptr}_n(x)=(1_{n-1}\\otimes\\cap)\\circ(x\\otimes1_1)\\circ(1_{n-1}\\otimes\\cup),\\qquad x\\in\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta).$$\n\nIt is a map $\\mathrm{TL}_n\\to\\mathrm{TL}_{n-1}$. If $\\delta$ is a unit, define $\\tau_n=\\delta^{-n}\\operatorname{Tr}_n$. This agrees with the normalized trace of [[def-temperley-lieb-normalized-markov-trace-by-closure]] over $\\mathbb C$ when $\\delta\\ne0$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-temperley-lieb-generators-satisfy-local-relations",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Fix $n\\ge0$, a commutative ring $R$, and $\\delta\\in R$. For $1\\le i<n$, let $d_i\\in\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta)$ be the elementary cup-cap diagram of [[def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category]]. Then\n\n$$d_i^2=\\delta d_i\\ (1\\le i<n),\\qquad d_i d_{i+1}d_i=d_i,\\quad d_{i+1}d_i d_{i+1}=d_{i+1}\\ (1\\le i\\le n-2),\\qquad d_i d_j=d_jd_i\\ (1\\le i,j<n,\\ |i-j|>1).$$\n\nConsequently the assignment $u_i\\mapsto d_i$ extends to a unital $R$-algebra homomorphism\n\n$$\\pi_n:P_n(R,\\delta)\\longrightarrow\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta).$$",
