      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "For a state with $k$ B-smoothings, the smoothed braid is the closure of a stack with $k$ copies of $e_1$ and $3-k$ identity layers, because each A-smoothing is $I$ by [F2]. If $k=0$, the identity closure has two circles by [F3]. If $k\\ge1$, the first $e_1$ connects the two closing arcs into one circle; each additional $e_1$ contributes one removed loop by $e_1^2=\\delta e_1$ in [F4]. Thus the state has $k$ circles. There are $\\binom{3}{k}$ states with $k$ B-smoothings, each with weight $A^{3-2k}\\delta^{|S|-1}$. The complete state table is $$\\begin{array}{c|c|c|l} k & \\text{states} & \\text{circles} & \\text{total contribution} \\\\ \\hline 0 & 1 & 2 & A^3\\delta \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & 3A \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 3A^{-1}\\delta \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & A^{-3}\\delta^2 \\end{array}$$ Each term follows from [F1] and the circle counts in [F3–F4].",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F4",
            "construct"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "Substituting $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$ into the table gives $$\\begin{aligned} \\langle D_+\\rangle &=A^3\\delta+3A+3A^{-1}\\delta+A^{-3}\\delta^2\\\\ &=(-A^5-A)+3A+(-3A-3A^{-3}) +(A+2A^{-3}+A^{-7})\\\\ &=A^{-7}-A^{-3}-A^5. \\end{aligned}$$ The braid has three positive crossings, so [F5] gives $\\operatorname{wr}(D_+)=3$. Therefore $$f_{D_+}(A)=(-A^3)^{-3}(A^{-7}-A^{-3}-A^5) =A^{-4}+A^{-12}-A^{-16}=t+t^3-t^4.$$ By [F6], this is the library Jones value.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
