        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "Mirroring keeps the projection and swaps over and under. To return the over-strand to the source chart's southwest-to-northeast position, rotate the local chart through a positive quarter-turn; this exchanges the top/bottom and left/right pairings. Thus the A- and B-smoothings interchange, so state-by-state $\\langle D_-\\rangle(A)=\\langle D_+\\rangle(A^{-1})$. The determinant sign changes sign when the over and under tangent vectors are exchanged, hence $\\operatorname{wr}(D_-)=-3$ by [F5]. It follows directly that $f_{D_-}(A)=f_{D_+}(A^{-1})=t^{-1}+t^{-3}-t^{-4}$, and [F6] identifies this with $V_{D_-}(t)$. By [F7], the crossing-free one-circle diagram has one state with one circle and writhe $0$, so its raw bracket is $1$ and [F6] gives $V_U(t)=1$.",
