          "source": "def-bmw-algebra-with-fixed-kauffman-skein-convention",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a commutative unital ring, let $q,\\rho\\in R^\\times$, put $z=q-q^{-1}$, and choose $\\delta\\in R$ with $z(\\delta-1)=\\rho-\\rho^{-1}$. For $n\\ge2$, the BMW algebra $BMW_n(R;q,\\rho,\\delta)$ is the unital associative $R$-algebra generated by invertible $g_i$ and elements $e_i$ for $1\\le i<n$, subject to the following relations (an adjacent relation is imposed only when both indices exist):\n\n- braid and distant braid: $g_i g_{i+1}g_i=g_{i+1}g_i g_{i+1}$ and $g_i g_j=g_jg_i$ for $|i-j|\\ge2$;\n- distant cups and caps: $g_i e_j=e_jg_i$ and $e_i e_j=e_j e_i$ for $|i-j|\\ge2$;\n- adjacent cup-cap: $e_i e_{i\\pm1}e_i=e_i$, $g_i g_{i\\pm1}e_i=e_{i\\pm1}e_i$, and $e_i g_{i\\pm1}g_i=e_i e_{i\\pm1}$;\n- Kauffman skein and untwisting: $g_i-g_i^{-1}=z(1-e_i)$, $g_i e_i=e_i g_i=\\rho^{-1}e_i$, and $e_i g_{i\\pm1}e_i=\\rho e_i$;\n- loop: $e_i^2=\\delta e_i$.\n\nFor the boundary ranks, set $BMW_0(R;q,\\rho,\\delta)=BMW_1(R;q,\\rho,\\delta)=R$, with the empty and single straight tangle as their respective units.\n\nIf $z$ is invertible, the parameter relation reads $\\delta=1+(\\rho-\\rho^{-1})/z$. If $z$ is not invertible, the presentation uses the universal coefficient relation $z(\\delta-1)=\\rho-\\rho^{-1}$ and does not divide by $z$. The quotient by the two-sided ideal generated by all $e_i$ is the cup-cap-zero Hecke quotient; this definition does not assert a BMW diagram-basis theorem or a BMW quantum-centralizer theorem.",
