          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $K\\subset\\mathbb R^3$ be the image of a compact smooth embedded circle, and let $E:N^\\perp K\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be the Euclidean normal-addition map $E(p,v)=p+v$. There is a real $\\varepsilon>0$ such that $E$ restricts to a diffeomorphism from $\\{(p,v):\\|v\\|<\\varepsilon\\}$ onto an open neighborhood $N_\\varepsilon$ of $K$. Moreover, $\\mathbb R^3\\setminus K$ strongly deformation retracts onto $\\mathbb R^3\\setminus N_\\varepsilon$ by pushing each nonzero normal vector radially to length $\\varepsilon$. The construction uses only a finite cover of the compact circle and no choice axiom.",
          "uses": [
