          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $L=K_1\\cup\\cdots\\cup K_r\\subset S^3$ be an\noriented link (a finite disjoint union of oriented smoothly embedded circles,\n[[def-oriented-link-in-s-three-and-ambient-isotopy]]) with $r\\ge1$ components,\nand let $X_L:=S^3\\setminus L$. Then $X_L$ is a connected smooth $3$-manifold\nwithout boundary, and in particular is path-connected, locally path-connected\nand semilocally simply connected; moreover $X_L$ has the homotopy type of a\nfinite CW complex\n([[def-cw-complex-with-closure-finiteness-and-weak-topology]]). Consequently the\ncovering-space classification\n([[thm-classification-of-connected-covering-spaces]]) applies to $X_L$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-classification-of-connected-covering-spaces",
          "source_section": "Statement",
