        {
          "id": "step-5.1",
          "claim": "The diagram has finitely many cube generators, so the sequences $j\\mapsto h_{i,j}$ and $j\\mapsto r_{i,j}(p)$ have finite support. Rewrite step 4.1 as $r_{i,k}(p)=h_{i,k+1}-r_{i,k+2}(p)$. For each parity of $k$, start above the largest supported reduced degree, where the latter term is zero, and recurse downward by two; this uniquely determines all reduced dimensions from the unreduced dimensions. Therefore $r_{i,j}(p)=r_{i,j}(q)$ in every bidegree. Finite-dimensional vector spaces with equal dimensions are isomorphic in each bidegree; only finitely many bidegrees occur, so these isomorphisms assemble without an infinite choice principle.",
