      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "By [F1], choose a finite sequence $D=D_0,D_1,\\ldots,D_r=D'$ of planar isotopies and oriented Reidemeister moves. For a Reidemeister step choose a marked point on an unchanged exterior arc and carry it to the corresponding arc on the other diagram. Such an arc exists: the move models contain a continuing strand meeting the boundary of their disk, and a closed regular link diagram continues that strand outside the disk. For a planar isotopy choose any mark and carry it by the isotopy. There are finitely many steps and every diagram is nonempty, so these are finite point choices, adding no choice hypothesis beyond [F1]. These auxiliary marks need not all lie on a single tracked component.",
