          "claim": "At the start of a step, [F3] identifies the current reduced group with the reduction at its chosen auxiliary mark, even if that mark lies on another component. For a Reidemeister move, [F2] then gives a bigraded cochain homotopy equivalence between the reductions at the two unchanged exterior marks. Its integral maps and contractions commute with the marked action before quotienting, and their explicit equations remain true over $\\mathbb F_2$. For a planar isotopy the relabeling of circles preserves that marked factor and every normalized degree. Thus each step supplies a bigraded cohomology isomorphism, followed if necessary by another fixed-diagram change of mark using [F3].",
