    "thm-property-p-for-nontrivial-knots": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-knot-surgery-first-homology-mayer-vietoris",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented $3$-sphere, choose a closed tubular neighborhood $N(K)$, and set $E_K=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$ and $T_K=\\partial E_K=\\partial N(K)$; assume $E_K$ is connected. Let $\\mu$ be the oriented boundary of a normal disk whose orientation, preceded by the oriented tangent to $K$, agrees with the orientation of $S^3$. Let $\\lambda$ be a simple closed curve on $T_K$ whose degree under the normal-tube projection $T_K\\to K$ is $+1$ and whose image in $H_1(E_K;\\mathbb Z)$ is zero; such a curve is a preferred longitude. Assume $([\\mu],[\\lambda])$ is an ordered basis of $H_1(T_K;\\mathbb Z)$. For coprime integers $p,q$ not both zero, let $E_K(p/q)$ be the filling whose attached solid-torus meridian maps to $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$. Then\n$$H_1(E_K(p/q);\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\begin{cases}\\mathbb Z/|p|\\mathbb Z,&p\\ne0,\\\\[2pt]\\mathbb Z,&p=0.\\end{cases}$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "prop-the-first-hurewicz-map-in-degree-one-is-abelianization",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every path-connected topological space $X$ and $x_0\\in X$, the Hurewicz map\n$$h:\\pi_1(X,x_0)\\longrightarrow H_1(X;\\mathbb Z)$$\nis surjective and has kernel $[\\pi_1(X,x_0),\\pi_1(X,x_0)]$. Hence it induces a natural isomorphism\n$$\\pi_1(X,x_0)^{\\mathrm{ab}}\\cong H_1(X;\\mathbb Z).$$\nThe proof is choice-free and requires no CW, separation, local path-connectivity or local simple-connectivity assumption.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-property-p-instanton-surgery-triangle-and-rank-input",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K\\subset S^3$ be a nontrivial smooth knot, and let $p,q$ be coprime integers with $|p|=1$ and $q\\ne0$. For the Dehn filling $Y_{p/q}=E_K(p/q)$ whose attached solid-torus meridian is identified with $p[\\mu]+q[\\lambda]$, the fundamental group $\\pi_1(Y_{p/q})$ admits a homomorphism to $SU(2)$ with noncyclic image.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
