      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For each $J\\in\\{K,K'\\}$, the boundary $T_J$ is a circle bundle over the connected knot $J$ with connected fibres, hence is connected: a separation would split the boundary into saturated open sets whose projections, by local bundle charts, separate $J$. By [F10], $E_J$ is a compact smooth orientable $3$-manifold with boundary $T_J$. Since $T_J$ is connected, it lies in one component of $E_J$. Any other component is boundaryless, hence lies in $\\operatorname{int}E_J$ and is open in $S^3$; it is also closed in $S^3$, since it is closed in $E_J$ and $E_J$ is closed in $S^3$ by [F10]. This contradicts connectedness of $S^3$. Thus both exteriors are connected and, being manifolds, path-connected.",
