        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-sl-two-root-of-unity-skein-parameter",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix an even integer $p\\ge4$ and a primitive $2p$-th root of unity $A\\in\\mathbb C$. Put\n\n$$\\zeta=A^2,\\qquad q=-\\zeta,\\qquad r=p/2,\\qquad \\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}=q+q^{-1}.$$\n\nThe coefficient field after specialization is $\\mathbb C$, and the Kauffman bracket loop coefficient is $\\delta$ in the framed-link relation $[L\\sqcup O]=\\delta[L]$. Define the quantum integers by $[0]=0$, $[1]=1$, and $[j+1]=\\delta[j]-[j-1]$ for $j\\ge1$. Since $q^2=A^4$ has order $r\\ge2$, these quantum integers also satisfy\n\n$$[j]=\\frac{q^j-q^{-j}}{q-q^{-1}}=(-1)^{j-1}\\frac{A^{2j}-A^{-2j}}{A^2-A^{-2}}.$$\n\nThe BHMV simple-label convention is the finite set\n\n$$\\mathcal J_p=\\{0,1,\\ldots,r-2\\}.$$\n\nThe pivotal loop and coefficient conventions throughout this page are the displayed $\\delta$ and $\\mathbb C$; no zero quantum integer is inverted.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-temperley-lieb-jones-wenzl-recursion-over-unit-denominators",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring with unit and let $\\delta\\in R$. Use the quantum integers $[0]=0$, $[1]=1$, $[r+1]=\\delta[r]-[r-1]$ of [[def-temperley-lieb-quantum-integers-and-quantum-characteristic]]. Put $p_0=1_0$ and $p_1=1_1$. For $r\\ge1$, if $p_r$ is defined and $[r+1]$ is a unit, put\n\n$$P_r=p_r\\otimes1_1\\in\\mathrm{TL}_{r+1}(R,\\delta),\\qquad p_{r+1}=P_r-\\frac{[r]}{[r+1]}P_rU_rP_r,$$\n\nwhere $U_r$ is the cap-cup generator on the final two of the $r+1$ strands in [[def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category]]. Thus $p_n$ is defined by this recursion only when every $[2],\\ldots,[n]$ is a unit. The definition makes no assertion that failure of a denominator condition prevents every other normalized projector from existing.\n\n```tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.9cm]\n  \\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.8);\n  \\draw (1,0) -- (1,1.8);\n  \\node[draw,minimum width=0.55cm,minimum height=0.45cm] at (0.5,1.25) {$p_r$};\n  \\node[draw,minimum width=0.55cm,minimum height=0.45cm] at (0.5,0.45) {$p_r$};\n  \\draw (2,0) -- (2,1.8);\n  \\draw (3,0) .. controls (3,0.55) and (2.75,0.75) .. (2.5,0.9);\n  \\draw (2,0) .. controls (2,0.55) and (2.25,0.75) .. (2.5,0.9);\n  \\draw (2.5,0.9) .. controls (2.75,1.05) and (3,1.25) .. (3,1.8);\n  \\draw (2.5,0.9) .. controls (2.25,1.05) and (2,1.25) .. (2,1.8);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n```\n\nThe box labels stand for the corresponding idempotents and the right-hand cup-cap is $U_r$; the picture is only a convention aid. All algebraic identities are proved from the labeled matching composition and the relations of [[lem-temperley-lieb-generators-satisfy-local-relations]].",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-temperley-lieb-jones-wenzl-partial-trace-and-uniqueness",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a nonzero commutative ring with unit, $\\delta\\in R$, and suppose $[2],\\ldots,[n]$ are units. The projector $p_n$ of [[def-temperley-lieb-jones-wenzl-recursion-over-unit-denominators]] has coefficient $1$ on the identity diagram, is nonzero and idempotent, and is annihilated on both sides by each $U_i$ for $1\\le i<n$. Its corner is $p_n\\mathrm{TL}_n p_n=R p_n$, so it is the unique idempotent with identity coefficient $1$ and those two-sided annihilation conditions. For $n\\ge1$,\n\n$$\\operatorname{ptr}_n(p_n)=\\frac{[n+1]}{[n]}p_{n-1},\\qquad \\operatorname{Tr}_n(p_n)=[n+1].$$\n\nOnly the displayed denominator units are assumed; $\\delta$ need not be a unit.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-temperley-lieb-closure-trace-component-identities",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For any commutative ring $R$, loop value $\\delta\\in R$, and $n\\ge0$, the unnormalized trace of [[def-temperley-lieb-closure-trace-and-partial-trace]] satisfies\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_n(xy)=\\operatorname{Tr}_n(yx),\\qquad \\operatorname{Tr}_{n+1}(x\\otimes1)=\\delta\\operatorname{Tr}_n(x)$$\n\nfor $x,y\\in\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta)$. For $n\\ge1$ and $x\\in\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta)$, it also satisfies\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_{n+1}((x\\otimes1)U_n)=\\operatorname{Tr}_n(x),$$\n\nwhere $U_n$ is the cup-cap generator on the last two strands of $\\mathrm{TL}_{n+1}$. For $n\\ge1$, $x\\in\\mathrm{TL}_{n-1}$ and $h\\in\\mathrm{TL}_n$,\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_n\\bigl(h(x\\otimes1)\\bigr)=\\operatorname{Tr}_{n-1}\\bigl(\\operatorname{ptr}_n(h)x\\bigr).$$\n\nNo division by $\\delta$ occurs.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
