          "quote": "Fix even $p\\ge4$, a primitive $2p$-th root $A$, and $r=p/2$. In the Temperley–Lieb diagram category over $\\mathbb C$ with loop value $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$, call $f:m\\to n$ negligible when $\\operatorname{Tr}_m(g\\circ f)=0$ for every reverse morphism $g:n\\to m$, where $\\operatorname{Tr}$ is the unnormalized diagram-closure trace. A tensor ideal is a family of linear subspaces of the morphism spaces closed under composition on either side and tensor product on either side by arbitrary morphisms. The negligible morphisms form a tensor ideal. This ideal is generated, as a tensor ideal, by the Jones–Wenzl projector $p_{r-1}$, defined by the standard recursion through its first zero quantum integer; in particular the quotient has precisely the surviving projector labels $0,\\ldots,r-2$.",
