          "quote": "For every $\\ell\\ge3$, let $\\mathcal T_\\ell$ be the full finite-dimensional integrable type-1 tilting category of [[def-temperley-lieb-rank-one-lusztig-tilting-category]], and $\\mathcal N_\\ell$ its negligible ideal. The quotient with the same objects and morphism spaces $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal T_\\ell}(X,Y)/\\mathcal N_\\ell(X,Y)$ is a finite semisimple ribbon category. Its simple objects are exactly $T(0),\\ldots,T(\\ell-2)$, of pivotal dimensions $[a+1]_q$, and\n\n$$[T(a)][T(b)]=\\sum_{\\substack{|a-b|\\le c\\le\\min(a+b,2\\ell-4-a-b)\\\\c\\equiv a+b\\ (2)}}[T(c)]\\qquad(0\\le a,b\\le\\ell-2).$$\n\nHere a fusion category means a $\\mathbb C$-linear rigid semisimple monoidal category with simple unit and finitely many simple isomorphism classes. The quotient is spherical with the specified positive pivotal dimensions and inherits the full ribbon structure, including even $\\ell$.",
