    "lem-root-skein-surgery-kirby-color-invariance": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-sl-two-root-of-unity-skein-parameter",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix an even integer $p\\ge4$ and a primitive $2p$-th root of unity $A\\in\\mathbb C$. Put\n\n$$\\zeta=A^2,\\qquad q=-\\zeta,\\qquad r=p/2,\\qquad \\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}=q+q^{-1}.$$\n\nThe coefficient field after specialization is $\\mathbb C$, and the Kauffman bracket loop coefficient is $\\delta$ in the framed-link relation $[L\\sqcup O]=\\delta[L]$. Define the quantum integers by $[0]=0$, $[1]=1$, and $[j+1]=\\delta[j]-[j-1]$ for $j\\ge1$. Since $q^2=A^4$ has order $r\\ge2$, these quantum integers also satisfy\n\n$$[j]=\\frac{q^j-q^{-j}}{q-q^{-1}}=(-1)^{j-1}\\frac{A^{2j}-A^{-2j}}{A^2-A^{-2}}.$$\n\nThe BHMV simple-label convention is the finite set\n\n$$\\mathcal J_p=\\{0,1,\\ldots,r-2\\}.$$\n\nThe pivotal loop and coefficient conventions throughout this page are the displayed $\\delta$ and $\\mathbb C$; no zero quantum integer is inverted.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-semisimplified-temperley-lieb-fusion-category",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix an even integer $p\\ge4$, a primitive $2p$-th root $A\\in\\mathbb C$, $r=p/2$, and loop value $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$. Let $\\mathcal T_\\delta$ be the complex Temperley–Lieb diagram category with objects the nonnegative integers and morphisms finite linear combinations of perfect matchings of bottom and top boundary points with no intersecting arcs. Compose by stacking and remove each closed component with factor $\\delta$. Define $\\mathcal N_\\delta(m,n)$ to be the subspace of morphisms $f:m\\to n$ such that $\\operatorname{Tr}_m(g\\circ f)=0$ for every reverse morphism $g:n\\to m$, where $\\operatorname{Tr}$ is the unnormalized diagram-closure trace. Form the quotient category with the same objects and morphism spaces $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal T_\\delta}(m,n)/\\mathcal N_\\delta(m,n)$. Its additive envelope adjoins finite formal direct sums, with matrix morphisms and matrix composition. Its idempotent completion adjoins objects $(X,e)$ for idempotents $e\\in\\operatorname{End}(X)$ with $e^2=e$, and morphisms $(X,e)\\to(Y,f)$ are morphisms $a:X\\to Y$ satisfying $a=fae$. Juxtaposition, planar cup-cap duality, and the induced trace descend to this completed quotient. This definition makes no assertion that it is semisimple, that its simple objects have a specified label set, or that any braid, twist, or modularity identities hold.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-root-fusion-rules-and-simple-object-completeness",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $p\\ge4$ be even, $A\\in\\mathbb C$ a primitive $2p$-th root, and $r=p/2$. In the BHMV Temperley–Lieb quotient with loop value $\\delta=-A^2-A^{-2}$ and planar pivotal trace, the complete simple-label set is $\\{0,1,\\ldots,r-2\\}$, represented by the surviving Jones–Wenzl projectors $p_a$ obtained from the standard recursion using unit denominators $[2],\\ldots,[a]$. Every simple is self-dual. Its fusion multiplicities are\n\n$$N_{ab}^{c}=1 \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad |a-b|\\le c\\le\\min(a+b,\\,2r-4-a-b) \\ \\text{and }a+b+c\\text{ is even},$$\n\nand are zero otherwise. With the BHMV overcrossing map $c_i=A1_i+A^{-1}U_i$, where $U_i$ is the cup-cap generator, the full-framing ribbon structure has planar quantum dimensions $d_a=[a+1]$ and simple-object twists $\\theta_a=(-1)^aA^{a(a+2)}$. Here the quantum integers use the fixed BHMV recurrence. The unnormalized Hopf-link matrix, whose $(a,b)$ entry is the pivotal trace of the double braiding on $p_a\\otimes p_b$, is nondegenerate. Here modular means that this finite semisimple ribbon category has an invertible unnormalized Hopf-link matrix.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-extended-skein-cobordism-anomaly-data",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For the fixed root parameter, let $\\mathcal C_p$ denote the semisimplified Temperley–Lieb category with labels $0,\\ldots,r-2$, pivotal dimensions $d_j=[j+1]$, and Hopf-link data inherited from the Kauffman bracket. Put $\\mathcal D_p^2=\\sum_{j=0}^{r-2}d_j^2$ and choose $\\mathcal D_p\\in\\mathbb C$ with that square. Choose $\\kappa\\in\\mathbb C$ satisfying $\\kappa^6=A^{-6-(p+1)p/2}$. The root-specific extended data are the weighted Lagrangian ribbon bordisms whose objects are closed oriented labeled surfaces with a Lagrangian subspace of real first homology and whose morphisms are collared oriented labeled ribbon bordisms with integer weights. If $M_1:\\Sigma_0\\to\\Sigma_1$ and $M_2:\\Sigma_1\\to\\Sigma_2$ have relations $\\Lambda_{M_1},\\Lambda_{M_2}$ and boundary Lagrangians $\\lambda_0,\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2$, define\n\n$$K_1=\\Lambda_{M_1}(\\lambda_0),\\qquad K_0=\\lambda_1,\\qquad K_2=\\Lambda_{M_2}^{\\,t}(\\lambda_2), \\qquad n(M_2\\circ M_1)=n_2+n_1+\\mu(K_1,K_0,K_2),$$\n\nusing the Wall-signature Maslov convention. The category composition, units, and anomaly weight are those specified by this formula and the weighted Lagrangian bordism definition; no ordinary oriented anomaly-free functor is part of this Definition.",
