          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Choice** (AC) is the following statement.\n\n> Every family of nonempty sets has a choice function\n> (Choice function).\n\nWritten out: for every set $\\mathcal{F}$ all of whose members are nonempty,\nthere exists a function $g$ with domain $\\mathcal{F}$ satisfying $g(S) \\in S$ for\nall $S \\in \\mathcal{F}$.\n\nAn equivalent formulation is that a product of nonempty sets is nonempty: if\n$X_i \\ne \\emptyset$ for every $i \\in I$, then $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i \\ne \\emptyset$.\nHere $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i$ is the set of functions $f$ with domain $I$ such that\n$f(i) \\in X_i$ for every $i \\in I$; when a family of nonempty sets is indexed by\nitself, such an $f$ is precisely a choice function for it.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "2.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-kirby-moves-classify-framed-link-presentations",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $D_0$ and $D_1$ be finite integral framed-link surgery diagrams in the standard oriented $3$-sphere, with surgery results $M_0$ and $M_1$. Then $M_0$ and $M_1$ are orientation-preservingly diffeomorphic if and only if $D_0$ and $D_1$ are related by a finite sequence of ambient isotopies, framed handle slides, and additions or deletions of split $\\pm1$-framed unknots.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-root-skein-surgery-kirby-color-invariance",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Fix even $p\\ge4$, a primitive $2p$-th root $A$, the BHMV semisimplified category, and its quantum dimensions $d_j$ and twists $\\theta_j$ for $0\\le j\\le r-2$. Put $\\Omega_p=\\sum_{j=0}^{r-2}d_jp_j$, $\\Delta_+=\\sum_jd_j^2\\theta_j$, and $\\Delta_-=\\sum_jd_j^2\\theta_j^{-1}$. The Statement asserts that both $\\Delta_+$ and $\\Delta_-$ are nonzero. For a finite integral framed link $L$ in the oriented three-sphere, color each surgery component by $\\Omega_p$ and normalize the bracket evaluation by $\\Delta_+^{b_+(L)}\\Delta_-^{b_-(L)}$, where $b_\\pm(L)$ are the positive and negative indices of the framing matrix. With the stated BHMV root and weighted anomaly convention, the resulting value is unchanged under framed isotopy, handle slides, and addition or deletion of a split $\\pm1$-framed unknot.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
