          "claim": "**Construct the smooth handle basis and its intersection matrix.** Cap the single boundary component by a disk and apply [F1] to obtain the oriented polygon normal form $\\prod_{h=1}^g[a_h,b_h]$; remove the capping disk to recover the one-boundary surface. In this model the $h$th handle has two standard core curves, one meridional and one longitudinal, which meet once. Choose their orientations so the ordered tangent pair is positive at that crossing; curves from distinct handles are disjoint. The finite chart and disk-band construction in [F1] realizes this model on the given smooth surface: draw the curves as finite piecewise-smooth arcs in its bands and smooth their finitely many corners in disjoint coordinate disks, leaving their crossings fixed. In the model the surface retracts to the graph of these $2g$ core generators, so their homology classes form an integral basis; the same is true on $F$. Their intersection matrix is therefore the block sum $J_0=\\bigoplus_{h=1}^g\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&0\\end{pmatrix}$, with zero entries between distinct handles.",
