          "quote": "Assume countable choice. For every smooth oriented knot $K$ in $S^3$, there are an oriented normal-bundle trivialization, a tubular map $\\Phi$ defined on an open neighbourhood containing $S^1\\times D^2_{2\\epsilon}$ for some $\\epsilon>0$, and a closed tubular neighbourhood $N(K)=\\Phi(S^1\\times D^2_\\epsilon)$. This $N(K)$ is diffeomorphic to $S^1\\times D^2$, its boundary $T_K$ is diffeomorphic to $S^1\\times S^1$, and its exterior $E_K=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$ is a compact smooth oriented three-manifold with boundary $T_K$. The open complement $S^3\\setminus K$ strongly deformation retracts onto $E_K$.",
