          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented knot in the oriented standard three-sphere, and let $F$ be a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface with boundary orientation equal to that of $K$. Let $g\\ge0$ satisfy $\\chi(F)=1-2g$. Choose a small product tubular neighborhood $N(K)$ adapted to the inward conormal of $F$, put $E=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$ and $S=F\\cap E$, and cut $E$ open along a product bicollar of $S$ to obtain the compact cut-open complement $Y$. Orient the normal line $n$ of $F$ by requiring $(n,u,v)$ to be positive in $S^3$ whenever $(u,v)$ is a positive tangent basis of $F$; name the face on the $+n$ side $S_+$ and the face on the $-n$ side $S_-$. Let $j:S\\hookrightarrow F$ be the collar-removal inclusion and $\\iota_\\pm:S\\to Y$ the two face inclusions; the inclusion induces an isomorphism on $H_1$, and set $i_\\pm=(\\iota_\\pm)_*\\circ j_*^{-1}$. Form $\\widetilde E_F$ from copies $Y_n$ by gluing $S_-(Y_n)$ to $S_+(Y_{n+1})$, and let $t:Y_n\\to Y_{n+1}$ be the deck shift. Because the boundary orientation of $F$ agrees with $K$, this shift is the positive-meridian shift. Let $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ be an ordered integral basis of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ and let $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$, where $a_i^+$ is the positive normal push-off. In the linking-dual basis given by $[\\gamma]\\mapsto([a]\\mapsto\\operatorname{lk}(\\gamma,a))$ under $H_1(Y;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\operatorname{Hom}(H_1(F;\\mathbb Z),\\mathbb Z)$, the map $i_- - t i_+$ is represented over $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t^{\\pm1}]$ by $V-tV^T$. Consequently $H_1(\\widetilde E_F;\\mathbb Z)$ is the cokernel of $V-tV^T$.",
