      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Regard the grid torus as the standard Heegaard torus separating the two solid tori of $S^3$, with horizontal circles meridians of the first and vertical circles meridians of the second. The $n$ parallel meridian disks in either solid torus cut it into $n$ balls, one for each row or column annulus. Push the row $O$-to-$X$ arcs into the first solid torus and the column $X$-to-$O$ arcs into the second. Their pushing disks lie in disjoint row or column annuli and are disjoint from the compression disks, so each arc system is simultaneously boundary parallel as required by [F2]. The over/under convention is vertical over horizontal, exactly [F1]'s link. Thus these data represent the same oriented knot and satisfy the topological part of the multipointed definition; it remains to prove its admissibility condition.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
