        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Let $p_{ij}$ be the coefficient of cell $R_{ij}$ in a periodic domain $P$. Because $\\partial P$ is a sum of whole horizontal and vertical circles, the coefficient jump across a vertical circle is independent of the row, and the jump across a horizontal circle is independent of the column. Fix reference indices $i_0,j_0$ and set $a_i=p_{i,j_0}$ and $b_j=p_{i_0,j}-p_{i_0,j_0}$. Summing the constant jumps from the reference row and column gives $p_{ij}=a_i+b_j$ for every cell. Since the marking permutation in [F1] is one cycle, number its basepoint pairs in reverse order of knot travel so that row region $A_i$ contains $w_i,z_i$ and column region $B_i$ contains $w_i,z_{i+1}$, as allowed by the convention in [F2]. Then $P=\\sum_i a_iA_i+\\sum_i b_iB_i$, with local multiplicities $n_{w_i}(P)=a_i+b_i$ and $n_{z_i}(P)=a_i+b_{i-1}$.",
