          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "A knot grid is nonempty. Apply [F1] to each $G_i$, obtaining a finite grid-move sequence to a bridge-like grid $B_i$. Smooth $B_i$ as in that supplier to a bridge diagram $D_i$. Its crossing decorations and strand orientation agree with the original grid diagram, and the supplier proves planar isotopy after smoothing. Thus $D_0,D_1$ represent the same oriented knot. The three-mark splits and strict interval commutations in [F1] are among those specified here: the retained exterior row and column partners provide the two markings outside the stabilization block in the Statement. No unlisted shared-endpoint switch has been used.",
