    "lem-heegaard-floer-holomorphic-disk-regularity-compactness-gluing": {
      "risk": "high",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-balanced-knot-data-admit-full-marked-square-zero-holomorphic-counts",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Fix an actual balanced multipointed Heegaard diagram for an oriented knot in $S^3$, with $k\\ge1$ cyclically ordered mark pairs, $m=h+k-1$, transverse attaching systems and complete compression disks cutting the two handlebodies into $k$ balls. Broad auxiliary proper disk witnesses are permitted. Label the cut components by $A_i$ containing $w_i,z_i$ and $B_i$ containing $w_i,z_{i+1}$, cyclically.\n\nThere is a choice of integrable surface background, protected nearly symmetric geometry, common exact generator charts and ONE smooth tame path constant on genuine positive time collars, with no nonconstant strip of index at most zero, for which every actual nonconstant strip of index one or two is regular and there are finitely many index-one translation orbits across ALL generators, realized classes and nonnegative $w,z$ vectors. No $n_z=0$ restriction is imposed. Its endpoint unit boundary disks are regular and finite at every generator. Their mod-two counts are one for each $A_i,B_i$ when $k\\ge2$, and zero for the single alpha and beta components when $k=1$; in the latter case unit spheres through the generators are excluded as in the singly pointed construction.\n\nLet $C$ be the free module on the finite generator set over $\\mathbb F_2[U_1,\\ldots,U_k]$. The ACTUAL differential\n$$d x=\\sum_{y,\\,[u]\\in\\widehat{\\mathcal M}_1(x,y)}U_1^{n_{w_1}(u)}\\cdots U_k^{n_{w_k}(u)}\\,y$$\ncounts all the above index-one orbits, including every positive $z$ multiplicity. It is a finite polynomial matrix, $d^2=0$, and it preserves the relative Alexander filtration with each $U_i$ lowering filtration by one. Identifying or localizing variables by any ring homomorphism preserves this identity.\n\nFor $k\\ge2$, retaining separate $V_i$ weights for $z_i$ gives the actual full-marked curvature identity\n$$D^2=\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^kU_i(V_i+V_{i+1})\\right)I.$$\nFor $k=1$ the corresponding full-marked $D$ has $D^2=0$ by the zero unit counts. These are chosen-data analytic count identities. Comparison to other paths or diagrams, absolute gradings, analytic/combinatorial identification and Floer invariance are not input or conclusion.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "3.1",
            "4.1",
            "5.1",
            "6.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-full-marked-index-two-compactification-gives-the-boundary-disk-curvature-identity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Use the actual balanced $S^3$ knot data with $k\\ge1$ and THE chosen surface complex structure and genuine constant-collar path constructed in the corresponding multipointed or singly pointed full-marked low-index count theorem, whose construction excludes every nonconstant strip of index at most zero as well as giving full-marked index-one and index-two regularity and finite counts. For $k=1$ this is the sphere-avoiding path from the singly pointed theorem. Label the individual cut components so $A_i$ contains $w_i,z_i$ and $B_i$ contains $w_i,z_{i+1}$, with cyclic indices.\n\nFor fixed generators $x,y$ and nonnegative integer vectors $W,Z$, let $\\widehat{\\mathcal M}_2(x,y;W,Z)$ consist of ALL actual index-two strips with these ends and marked-degree vectors, modulo longitudinal translation, across all realized Whitney classes. This is a Hausdorff second-countable topological one-manifold. It has a compactification as a compact one-manifold with finite boundary, whose boundary points are exactly:\n\n1. Ordered pairs of actual rigid index-one strip orbits with matched intermediate generator and marked vectors summing to $W,Z$.\n2. When $x=y$, the actual unit $A_i$ or $B_i$ boundary-disk orbits with boundary node value $x$ and the prescribed marked vector, attached to the constant generator strip.\n\nEach point has the actual exhaustive one-sided gluing collar of its respective type. No extra boundary points occur, and no differentiability at a prescribed compactifying parameter is asserted.\n\nLet $a_i(x),b_i(x)\\in\\mathbb F_2$ be the actual finite node-fixed affine-orbit counts of the $A_i,B_i$ disks at $x$. On the free module generated by the generators over $R=\\mathbb F_2[U_1,\\ldots,U_k,V_1,\\ldots,V_k]$, define $D$ by the actual finite rigid-strip counts with weight $U^{n_w}V^{n_z}$. Then\n$$D^2x=\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^k a_i(x)U_iV_i+\\sum_{i=1}^k b_i(x)U_iV_{i+1}\\right)x.$$\nSetting every $V_i=1$ gives the actual f