          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let complete balanced disk systems of rank $m=h+k-1$ on a genus-h surface belong to ONE specified handlebody, with one w and one z mark in every cut component, and with the same actual trivial arcs and marks. Realize a specified own-system handleslide and its sufficiently small auxiliary copies by the circular ribbon model of the named suppliers; take the other curve copies sufficiently small. A handleslide requires $m\\ge2$. Small isotopy copies alone are allowed for $m\\ge1$. The actual ribbon and its common exterior avoid all marks.\n\nThe full marked index-one differential of each required model pair kills its top generator. Both actual top-input, index-zero triangle products in the circular move construction equal the stated top output with coefficient one, with NO other output or positive marked term. These assertions hold over the polynomial ring with all individual w and z variables retained, and hence after setting every z variable equal to one. They hold for sufficiently small regular coherent protected perturbations of the model.\n\nThis applies to every actual balanced h,k, including dependent meridian lists and genus zero when the required number of curves exists. No inference is made about mixed-system triangles involving the opposite handlebody. The proof computes actual zero-Chern restrictions and same-corner index differences; it does not assume every formal degree-one periodic domain has a Whitney representative.",
