connected generator set. In an actual full filtered minus differential, including positive multiplicities at both basepoints, the term $U^{n_w(\\phi)}y$ has Alexander level $A_F(x)-n_z(\\phi)$. An exact finite matrix model of that diagram acquires its absolute grading by evaluating this Euler number at one generator and then using the relative differences. This last assertion does not claim that an uncalibrated numerical matrix or the relative grading alone already supplies that Euler evaluation. In particular, if an actual orientation-preserving diagram isomorphism exchanges the two marks, followed by a mark-free attaching-curve isotopy returning its generator to $y$ in the original diagram, then $A_F(x)=-A_F(y)$. If the relative calculation also gives $A_F(x)=A_F(y)$, both are zero. Arbitrary Heegaard-move comparison and a grid closed-form centering calculation are separate operations.",
