          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Supply an embedded admissible DOUBLY pointed diagram for an oriented knot $K$ in the standard oriented three-sphere, its compression disks and compatible Morse trajectory data, and a compact oriented Seifert surface $F$. Use the knot orientation from $w$ to $z$ in the alpha handlebody and from $z$ to $w$ in the beta handlebody. In positive genus let $x$ be a generator. In genus zero use the empty generator. There is an actual relative knot Spin-c lift $t_{w,z}(x)$ on the zero surgery $S^3_0(K)$, constructed with the following convention: on the knot exterior use the NEGATIVE of the compatible gradient after cancelling the index-one/index-two trajectories selected by $x$; across the zero-surgery solid torus use the zero-relative-Euler extension specified in the proof. Reversing this vector field convention would reverse its Alexander evaluation and is not silently permitted.\n\nThe integer\n$$A_F(x)=\\frac12\\langle c_1(t_{w,z}(x)),[\\widehat F]\\rangle$$\nis well defined, independent of the local extension and framing choices in that construction and of the choice of Seifert surface for the fixed oriented knot. For every actual Whitney class from $x$ to $y$,\n$$A_F(x)-A_F(y)=n_z(\\phi)-n_w(\\phi).$$\nThe standard genus-zero unknot generator has value zero. The construction is carried by orientation-preserving isomorphisms of the supplied knot, surface and Morse data, and by a smooth mark-free attaching-curve isotopy with its followed generator. Swapping $w,z$ with the same underlying attaching systems gives $A_{z,w}(x)=-A_{w,z}(x)$; this is a statement about the actual Chern pairing, not a homological symmetry theorem. Its value can be computed as half the relative Euler number of the exterior perpendicular plane on $F\\setminus N(K)$ with the explicit boundary frame in the proof; the solid-torus cap contributes zero.\n\nConsequently this construction fixes the additive constant of the relative Alexander grading on every connected generator set. In an actual full filtered minus differential, including positive multiplicities at both basepoints, the term $U^{n_w(\\phi)}y$ has Alexander level $A_F(x)-n_z(\\phi)$. An exact finite matrix model of that diagram acquires its absolute grading by evaluating this Euler number at one generator and then using the relative differences. This last assertion does not claim that an uncalibrated numerical matrix or the relative grading alone already supplies that Euler evaluation. In particular, if an actual orientation-preserving diagram isomorphism exchanges the two marks, followed by a mark-free attaching-curve isotopy returning its generator to $y$ in the original diagram, then $A_F(x)=-A_F(y)$. If the relative calculation also gives $A_F(x)=A_F(y)$, both are zero. Arbitrary Heegaard-move comparison and a grid closed-form centering calculation are separate operations.",
