          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The marking permutation sends the $O$ in row $0$ to the $X$ in column $1$ and then to the $O$ in row $1$; it continues from row $1$ through column $2$ to row $2$, and from row $2$ through column $0$ back to row $0$. Thus the grid has one component. In its planar projection the oriented path has vertices $(0.5,0.5),(1.5,0.5),(1.5,1.5),(2.5,1.5),(2.5,2.5),(0.5,2.5)$ and returns to $(0.5,0.5)$. These six axis-parallel edges form a simple polygon and meet only at consecutive endpoints, so the projection has no crossings and is an unknot diagram.",
