          "source": "thm-complete-pointed-heegaard-diagrams-admit-globally-weak-admissible-isotopies",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Give any actual complete singly pointed Heegaard diagram of a closed connected oriented smooth three-manifold $Y$ as in [[def-hat-heegaard-floer-complex-of-a-closed-three-manifold]], with transverse attaching systems and basepoint $z$. There is a finite sequence of smooth isotopies of individual alpha circles, avoiding $z$ and the other alpha circles, after which opposite systems are again transverse and EVERY nonzero integral periodic region domain with $n_z=0$ has both positive and negative coefficients. The same splitting surface, manifold, basepoint and beta system are retained; the alpha system still bounds a complete compression-disk system.\n\nThus globally weakly admissible diagrams can be chosen for every such complete splitting, for general $Y$. Neither a rational homology sphere nor a torsion Spin-c premise is imposed. This is the global condition, stronger than ordinary weakness in ONE specified sector. The input here is an arbitrary complete geometric diagram; it is not asserted to satisfy that condition before the isotopies. The corrected full-module admissibility convention is equivalent to global weakness, whereas a specified-sector-only construction remains separate. No count invariance along the isotopies, sector-index theorem, strong Spin-c admissibility or Floer move map is asserted.",
