        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-based-heegaard-moves-generate-closed-three-manifold-diagram-equivalence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Any two actual pointed Heegaard diagrams of the same closed connected oriented smooth three-manifold are related by a finite sequence of attaching-curve isotopies and same-system handleslides avoiding the basepoint, genus stabilizations and destabilizations in basepoint-disjoint disks, and orientation-preserving embedded-diagram isomorphisms carrying the two handlebodies, surface, attaching systems and basepoint. Genus zero and empty attaching systems are included. The input compression witnesses may be proper in the broad smooth sense without boundary transversality.\n\nEvery intermediate diagram is a complete pointed Heegaard diagram of that same manifold: a genus-$g$ surface with $g$ disjoint compression disks cutting each handlebody into one ball. The theorem is purely geometric. It does not assert admissibility of every intermediate diagram, analytic maps, auxiliary-choice invariance, gradings or a comparison of complexes. No knot or extra basepoint is required in the input or retained in the conclusion.",
