          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-globally-weak-zero-marked-polygons-have-finite-counts-and-a-infinity-boundaries",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Use the coherent all-index regular data of the named supplier on a finite globally weak triple-free pointed multidiagram of rank $m\\ge1$, with a basepoint in every one-system cut component. Fix any finite maximum arity. Label a polygon with $d$ incoming corners by $x_i\\in L_{i-1}\\cap L_i$, $1\\le i\\le d$, and output $y\\in L_0\\cap L_d$. Its positive boundary-edge order is $L_0,L_d,L_{d-1},\\ldots,L_1$. Thus at an incoming corner the boundary traversal is $L_i\\to L_{i-1}$; the incoming strip has $t=0$ on $L_{i-1}$ and $t=1$ on $L_i$. All counts are over $\\mathbb F_2$ and impose zero multiplicity at every basepoint.\n\nFor $d\\ge2$ the actual polygon count dimension is $\\mu+d-2$; there is no triangle translation quotient. Its zero-dimensional total moduli are finite across ALL literal realized classes. Its one-dimensional total moduli compactify to compact one-manifolds whose boundaries are exactly the rigid polygon–polygon conformal splittings and rigid strip–polygon external breakings. Every such pair with matching generator has its actual exhaustive collar. No sphere, one-torus disk, constant polygon or additional escape stratum occurs. The same assertions hold after restricting to any actual class, using its actual concatenation rule.\n\nLet $m_1$ count unparametrized index-one strips and, for $d\\ge2$, let $m_d$ count polygons of fixed-map index $2-d$ with their $d-2$ conformal parameters. These finite maps satisfy the actual A-infinity identities\n$$\\sum_{r+s=d+1}\\ \\sum_{j=0}^{r-1}m_r(x_1,\\ldots,x_j,m_s(x_{j+1},\\ldots,x_{j+s}),x_{j+s+1},\\ldots,x_d)=0.$$\nHere $m_1$ on an output is included, and all label-compatible intermediate generators are summed. In particular the triangle map is a chain map and the quadrilateral count is its actual associativity homotopy.\n\nFor a generic coherent one-parameter triangle family with the same regular end strips, the universal index-minus-one moduli are finite; the universal index-zero moduli have compact one-dimensional boundary consisting of parameter endpoints and strip–triangle breakings. Their count gives the chain homotopy between the endpoint triangle maps. For rank $m=0$, the same count conclusions hold directly with the unique constant triangle counted once, zero differential, and all higher rigid operations zero. The source conformal boundary gives the same identities; no free strip-translation quotient is assigned to the constant point map.\n\nThis assertion concerns the supplied analytic choices, and does not assert a top-generator cycle, a Heegaard-move inverse, a Spin-c extension classification or filling identification.",
