          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Treat rank zero by [F3]'s direct model. Its map operator is the zero operator between zero spaces and is onto of index zero. A triangle has one matching constant map, no conformal parameter and no continuous automorphism. A higher stable polygon has its actual positive source dimension and no rigid contribution. The four-marked source is an interval whose two ends are the two constant triangle products, and its parity is zero over the coefficient field. A matching one-parameter triangle family is its parameter interval; other assigned labels or nonzero marked vectors give empty sets. There are no nonconstant strips or bubbles. This proves the point-target count identities without excluding an allowed genus-zero input.",
