          "claim": "Put $t=\\tau(C)$. By [F1], some class in $H(F_tC)$ maps to a nonzero class in $H(C)$. Since $f$ preserves filtration, its restriction sends $F_tC$ to $F_tD$. The square formed by these restricted maps and the inclusions into total complexes commutes, so the induced map sends that class to its image under $f_*$. The map $f_*$ is an isomorphism because $g_*$ is its homotopy inverse; hence the resulting class in $H(D)$ is nonzero. Therefore $H(F_tD)\\to H(D)$ has nonzero image and $\\tau(D)\\le t$.",
