          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "Put $q(u,v)=\\int_M(u\\overline v+\\nabla_Mu\\cdot\\overline{\\nabla_Mv})\\,dS$ on $H^1(M)$. For $f\\in L^2(M)$, [F2] gives a unique $u=\\widetilde Kf\\in H^1(M)$ with $q(u,v)=\\langle f,v\\rangle$ for every $v\\in H^1(M)$ and $\\|u\\|_{H^1}\\le\\|f\\|_2$. Let $J:H^1(M)\\hookrightarrow L^2(M)$ and $K=J\\widetilde K$. By step 2.1, $K$ is compact. Hermitian symmetry of $q$ gives $\\langle Kf,g\\rangle=\\langle f,Kg\\rangle$ and $\\langle Kf,f\\rangle=q(\\widetilde Kf,\\widetilde Kf)\\ge0$. If $Kf=0$, the weak equation and smooth density from step 1.1 imply $\\langle f,v\\rangle=0$ for every $v\\in L^2(M)$, so $f=0$. Thus $K$ is compact, positive, self-adjoint and injective.",
