          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "By [F3], $K$ has an orthonormal eigenbasis $e_j$ with positive eigenvalues $\\mu_j\\to0$; order these so that $\\mu_j$ is nonincreasing. Put $\\lambda_j=\\mu_j^{-1}-1$. From $Ke_j=\\mu_je_j$ and the weak equation, $\\int_M\\nabla_Me_j\\cdot\\overline{\\nabla_Mv}\\,dS=\\lambda_j\\langle e_j,v\\rangle$ for every $v\\in H^1(M)$. Taking $v=e_j$ gives $\\lambda_j=\\int_M|\\nabla_Me_j|^2\\,dS\\ge0$, and these are the eigenvectors of the stated weak Laplace–Beltrami operator. In the form inner product $q$, the vectors $(1+\\lambda_j)^{-1/2}e_j$ are orthonormal and complete: a vector $v$ orthogonal to every $e_j$ in $q$ satisfies $(1+\\lambda_j)\\langle v,e_j\\rangle=0$ for every $j$, hence vanishes in $L^2$. Form Parseval gives $q(v,v)=\\sum_j(1+\\lambda_j)|\\langle v,e_j\\rangle|^2$, proving the $s=1$ norm identity.",
