          "source": "thm-poincare-wirtinger-on-bounded-connected-extension-domains",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $n\\ge1$, let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be a\nnonempty bounded connected extension domain, and let $1\\le p<\\infty$. Then there is\n$C=C(\\Omega,p)$ such that every $u\\in W^{1,p}(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ satisfies\n$$\\|u-u_\\Omega\\|_{L^p(\\Omega)}\\le C\\|Du\\|_{L^p(\\Omega)},\\qquad u_\\Omega:=|\\Omega|^{-1}\\int_\\Omega u(x)\\,dx.$$",
