          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $M=\\partial\\Omega$ be the compact smooth boundary in the boundary spectral setting, let $P_0$ be projection onto $L^2_0(M)$, and let $T:L^2_0(M)\\to L^2_0(M)$ be Hilbert–Schmidt. Extend $T$ to $\\widetilde T:L^2(M)\\to L^2(M)$ by $\\widetilde T=\\iota_0TP_0$, where $\\iota_0$ is inclusion. Then there is a unique $\\kappa_T\\in L^2(M\\times M)$ such that\n$$\\widetilde T f(x)=\\int_M\\kappa_T(x,y)f(y)\\,dS_y\\quad\\text{for almost every }x\\text{ and every }f\\in L^2(M),$$\nand\n$$\\|\\kappa_T\\|_{L^2(M\\times M)}=\\|T\\|_{\\mathrm{HS}}.$$\nThe kernel has zero mean in each variable: $\\int_M\\kappa_T(x,y)\\,dS_y=0$ for almost every $x$, and $\\int_M\\kappa_T(x,y)\\,dS_x=0$ for almost every $y$.",
