          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $d\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset(0,1)^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected $C^1$ domain, let $0<m\\le M<\\infty$, and let $\\gamma\\in L^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb R)$ satisfy $m\\le\\gamma\\le M$ almost everywhere. Define $\\mathcal D(\\Omega):=H^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb C)/H_0^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb C)$ with its quotient norm. For every boundary trace class $f\\in\\mathcal D(\\Omega)$ there is a unique $u_{\\gamma,f}\\in f$ such that\n$$\\int_\\Omega\\gamma\\,\\nabla u_{\\gamma,f}\\cdot\\overline{\\nabla z}\\,dx=0\\qquad\\text{for every }z\\in H_0^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb C).$$\nFor every $g\\in\\mathcal D(\\Omega)$, the value $\\int_\\Omega\\gamma\\nabla u_{\\gamma,f}\\cdot\\overline{\\nabla V_g}\\,dx$ is independent of the representative $V_g\\in g$ and defines a bounded linear map $\\Lambda_\\gamma:\\mathcal D(\\Omega)\\to\\mathcal D(\\Omega)^*$. Constants are in its kernel and its range functionals annihilate constants.",
