      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Write $r=r_d\\ge0$, $n=d-1$ and $w_j=1+\\lambda_j$ on the total-mean-zero subspace. The counting estimate [F1] implies $w_j^{-1/2}\\le C(1+j)^{-1/n}$, after enlarging the constant for finitely many low modes. By [F5], $R=\\mathscr R_\\gamma$ maps the $L^2$ unit ball into a uniformly bounded $H^1_\\Delta$ ball. If $P_J$ is the first $J$-mode projection, then $R_J=P_JR$ has rank at most $J$ and $\\|R-R_J\\|\\le C(1+J)^{-1/n}$. Likewise $S=C_M^{r/2}$ has the rank-$J$ approximation $S_J=P_JS$ with $\\|S-S_J\\|\\le C(1+J)^{-r/n}$; for $r=0$ this means the bound one and does not assert that $S$ is compact.",
