          "source": "thm-ip-calderon-logarithmic-l2-stability",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. For each fixed integer $d\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset(0,1)^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected smooth domain, let $\\Omega'\\Subset\\Omega$, fix $m>0$, $M\\ge\\max\\{1,m\\}$, $R>0$ and $0<\\alpha<1$, and let $\\gamma,\\gamma_0\\in X_d(R)$. Set\n$$\\delta:=\\|\\dot{\\Lambda}_\\gamma-\\dot{\\Lambda}_{\\gamma_0}\\|_{\\mathcal L(\\mathcal D(\\Omega)/\\mathbb C\\mathbf1,(\\mathcal D(\\Omega)/\\mathbb C\\mathbf1)^*)}.$$\nThere exist constants $C>0$, $\\rho>0$ and $t_0\\in(0,1)$, depending only on $d,\\alpha,\\Omega,\\Omega',m,M,R$, such that\n$$\\|\\gamma-\\gamma_0\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}\\le C\\,\\omega(\\delta),\\qquad \\omega(0):=0,\\qquad \\omega(t):=\\left[\\log\\!\\left(\\frac1{\\min\\{t,t_0\\}}\\right)\\right]^{-\\rho}\\quad(t>0).$$\nHere $X_d(R)$ is the BV class when $d=2$ and the bounded $C^{1,\\alpha}$ class when $d\\ge3$, and $\\dot\\Lambda_\\gamma$ is the induced weak conductivity Dirichlet-to-Neumann map on the trace quotient by constants.",
          "uses": [
