          "source": "lem-ip-concave-modulus-hilbert-ball-intersection",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H_1,H_2$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $I$ be any set, let $x\\in H_1$, and let $(x_i)_{i\\in I}\\subset H_1$ and $(y_i)_{i\\in I}\\subset H_2$. Let $\\omega:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$ be continuous, nondecreasing and concave, with $\\omega(0)=0$. If\n$$\\|y_i-y_j\\|\\le\\omega(\\|x_i-x_j\\|)\\qquad(i,j\\in I),$$\nthen\n$$\\bigcap_{i\\in I}\\overline B\\bigl(y_i,\\omega(\\|x_i-x\\|)\\bigr)\\ne\\varnothing.$$\nThe intersection over an empty index set means all of $H_2$.",
