          "source": "lem-ip-ntd-smoothing-and-hilbert-schmidt-kernel-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice, let $d\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset(0,1)^d$ be nonempty, bounded, connected and $C^\\infty$, and let $\\gamma\\in X_d(R)$. Write $M=\\partial\\Omega$, $n=d-1$, and let $A_\\gamma$ and $\\widetilde A_\\gamma$ be the mean-zero smoothed NtD observation and its extension from the preceding definition. Then $\\widetilde A_\\gamma$ is Hilbert–Schmidt on $L^2(M)$ and has a unique zero-mean-in-each-variable kernel $\\kappa_\\gamma\\in L^2(M\\times M)$, with\n$$\\|\\kappa_\\gamma\\|_{L^2(M\\times M)}=\\|\\widetilde A_\\gamma\\|_{\\mathrm{HS}}.$$\nThe Hilbert–Schmidt norms are uniformly bounded over $X_d(R)$. Moreover, there is $C<\\infty$, depending only on the fixed class and domain, such that\n$$\\|\\dot\\Lambda_\\gamma-\\dot\\Lambda_{\\gamma_0}\\|_{\\mathcal L(\\dot{\\mathcal D},\\dot{\\mathcal D}^{*})}\\le C\\|\\kappa_\\gamma-\\kappa_{\\gamma_0}\\|_{L^2(M\\times M)}^{1/2}\\qquad(\\gamma,\\gamma_0\\in X_d(R)).$$",
