          "source": "lem-ip-meyers-higher-integrability-for-interior-conductivity-solutions",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $d\\ge2$, let $\\Omega$ be a bounded connected smooth domain, let $U\\Subset\\Omega$ be open, and fix $0<m\\le M<\\infty$. There are $p\\in(2,4)$ and $C<\\infty$, depending only on $d,m,M,\\Omega,U$, such that every real measurable $\\gamma$ with $m\\le\\gamma\\le M$ and every weak solution $u\\in H^1(\\Omega)$ of $\\operatorname{div}(\\gamma\\nabla u)=0$ satisfy\n$$\\|\\nabla u\\|_{L^p(U)}\\le C\\|\\nabla u\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}.$$\nIn particular, for a weak Neumann solution with quotient flux $F\\in\\dot{\\mathcal D}^{*}$, the right side is at most $C\\|F\\|_{\\dot{\\mathcal D}^{*}}$, uniformly in $\\gamma$.",
