          "claim": "Gluing the finitely many rectangles to disjoint boundary intervals of the disks and rounding the collar corners gives a smooth embedded compact two-manifold. The orientations agree along each attaching interval, so the surface is oriented. Outside a crossing neighborhood its boundary follows the original diagram arcs; inside each neighborhood the two long sides of the half-twisted band restore the specified crossing and its orientation. Hence the boundary is exactly the original oriented knot.",
