          "claim": "At each point of $K$, the inward unit vector in $T F$ perpendicular to $T K$ is a smooth nonzero normal vector. The orientation of $S^3$, the orientation of $K$, and the metric orient the normal plane; its positive quarter-turn supplies a smooth second unit vector. These vectors give an oriented orthonormal frame of the normal plane along all of $K$.",
