        {
          "id": "thm-seifert-zero-framing-and-framing-integer-1-2",
          "claim": "Let $s$ be the inward unit conormal, viewed in the round-metric normal bundle. By [F8], choose a smooth collar $c:K\\times[0,\\varepsilon_0)\\to F$ and orient its levels by the original $K$. For sufficiently small $\\delta>0$, set $J_0=c(K,\\delta)$. It is embedded, lies in $\\operatorname{int}F$, and is disjoint from $K$. No prescribed collar velocity is assumed: since $c$ is an embedding onto a boundary neighbourhood, $\\partial_t c(p,0)$ is inward transverse to $K$ in $F$. Its normal quotient is therefore $a(p)s(p)$ for a smooth function $a(p)>0$; a tangential component is allowed.",
