          "source": "thm-polygonal-jordan-curve",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "If $P\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ is a polygon, then $\\mathbb R^2\\setminus P$ has exactly two regions, one bounded and one unbounded, and\n\n$$\\operatorname{Fr}(U)=P$$\n\nfor each of them. Regions and frontiers are from [[def-plane-region-and-frontier]]. The proof uses the finite simple edge cycle of [[def-polygonal-arc-and-polygon]] and polygonal crossing parity from [[lem-polygonal-crossing-parity-is-locally-constant]].",
          "uses": [
